{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c48b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":160,"recorded_at":1780531400000315,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b348b79c3b79850ff49ec9615","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_results-ffb76b.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk results (RUN-260909-ffb76b, producer recovery + handoff)\n2|\n3|Scope: v0.6.0 selector contract (§§14.7/14.7.1, shared SelectionPlan\n4|construction/revalidation §14.7.2, refining §2.3, authoritative summaries\n5|§§5.7/14.7.3). Authority: spec v0.6.0 commit\n6|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6` (STORY-260908-18woqo landed).\n7|Branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns` at\n8|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`, descending from\n9|`origin/main` `8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653` (re-verified\n10|with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`). Candidate left UNCOMMITTED.\n11|No `ax` session surface exists in this tree; CLI delivery, wire exits,\n12|lifecycle effects, and the §14.7.4 recovery flow are caller/recovery-leaf\n13|owned. No product-code change was made in this run; see §1.\n14|\n15|## 1. Publication recovery record (this run)\n16|\n17|- `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-21gygk` returned\n18|  `refresh_already_current` (TrunkOID = ReviewedTrunkOID = `8cf4aaa…`,\n19|  BranchOID = `83640d1…`). The installed source fix restored the\n20|  previously missing immutable resource files: before this run the\n21|  worktree missed ~100 tracked `.task-board` files; after, 19\n22|  deletions + 3 modifications remain, all non-JSON board-checkout\n23|  artifacts (activity streams, progress/README markdown), none of them\n24|  product files and none covered by a validation gate.\n25|- Exact failed gate re-run on the final candidate:\n26|  `git ls-files -z '*.json' | xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c\n27|  'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` → exit 0\n28|  (122 tracked JSON files, all parse).\n29|- Product bytes untouched: zero product edits in this run. The working\n30|  candidate is exactly the RUN-260909-bd27d9 candidate: tracked delta\n31|  `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, `internal/sessrepo/store.go`,\n32|  `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go`; untracked `internal/sessquery/`\n33|  (13 files). sha256 (abbrev): LOGBOOK `da0823d6`, README `86af5b32`,\n34|  store.go `28d64e24`, sessrepo_test.go `a5618be2`, query.go `bde3c9c8`,\n35|  selector.go `6769455f`, plan.go `eaa82f3a`, revalidate.go `818df82e`,\n36|  digest.go `b6cc6a27`, TRACEABILITY.md `0fde2779`.\n37|- No stray `--help/` tree at the worktree root (verified absent); the\n38|  preserved prior-run artifact stays under gitignored\n39|  `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/stray/` and is not in the candidate diff.\n40|\n41|## 2. Validation re-derived by this run on the final candidate (real exits)\n42|\n43|| Command | Exit |\n44|| --- | --- |\n45|| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n46|| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n47|| `gofmt -l internal/sessquery/ internal/sessrepo/` (empty) | 0 |\n48|| `git diff --check -- internal/ LOGBOOK.md README.md` | 0 |\n49|| `go test ./... -count=1` (all 26 packages ok) | 0 |\n50|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` (91.0% / 87.6% / 92.2%) | 0 |\n51|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -race -count=1` | 0 |\n52|| tracked-JSON gate above | 0 |\n53|\n54|Raw logs: `TASK-260830-21gygk_validation-ffb76b.log` (attached).\n55|\n56|## 3. Mutation evidence (reused exact-candidate battery, machine manifest attached)\n57|\n58|No product byte changed since RUN-260909-bd27d9, so the battery was\n59|not repeated merely because a new run began. Machine manifest\n60|`TASK-260830-21gygk_mutants-bd27d9.json` (attached; 14 KiB) records,\n61|per mutant, the executed behavioral command\n62|(`go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v`) and\n63|the killing test names: 29 KILLED (26 narrowing `N-*`, 3 ordering\n64|`B-*`), 2 CONTROL green (`control-before`, `control-after`),\n65|`C-not-applied` NOT_APPLIED and `C-compile-failure`\n66|COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE — correctly distinguished, never counted\n67|as kills. Token-preserving grammar mutants (`N-first-at-split`,\n68|`N-local-prefix`, `N-id-case`, `N-peer-alias-fold`) were killed\n69|through the behavioral suites. Per-mutant logs\n70|(`mutants-bd27d9/*.log`, 11 MB) remain in worktree scratch\n71|`.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/mutants-bd27d9/` and are cited, not\n72|re-attached.\n73|\n74|## 4. Acceptance: 8 of 8 AC rows driven at the shared library boundary\n75|\n76|Unchanged code; matrix per `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`:\n77|\n78|1. Bare UUID/name selectors — `Reader.Resolve → resolveBare`\n79|   (`TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`,\n80|   `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`; repository entry\n81|   `Repository.Resolve` pinned by `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID`).\n82|2. Qualified selectors — `Reader.Resolve → resolveExplicit →\n83|   locateSource` (`TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex`,\n84|   `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack`,\n85|   `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource`,\n86|   `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`,\n87|   `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures`).\n88|3. Ambiguity — `matchName`, `selectIdentity`/`checkRecordAgreement`\n89|   (`TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`,\n90|   `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`,\n91|   `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions`).\n92|4. List summaries — `Reader.List → Repository.ListSessions →\n93|   Projector.Project` (`TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`,\n94|   `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`,\n95|   `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`). Whole-read refusal\n96|   on projection failure; no silent omit.\n97|5. Status summaries — `Reader.Status → Resolve → Projector.Project`,\n98|   `Reader.InspectLocal` (`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`\n99|   plus list tests and qualified status rows). Record-only chains keep\n100|   the accepted internal projection with empty owner/lease: per the\n101|   pinned prefix clarification this is an interrupted persistence\n102|   prefix for the §14.7.4 recovery leaf, not a public creating state\n103|   (SPEC §5.7 requires Session Record AND initial lease for creating;\n104|   §13.1 step 2 persists the initial Lease Record before process\n105|   creation). No nullable/placeholder owner or lease field added.\n106|6. Stable deterministic sorting — `Reader.read`, `peerCandidates`,\n107|   `selectIdentity` (order tests above plus\n108|   `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`).\n109|7. SelectionPlan build/revalidate — `Reader.BuildPlan → bindPlan`,\n110|   `Reader.Revalidate`, `ParsePlan`, `BoundariesFor`\n111|   (`TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange` per-member arms and 7\n112|   further plan tests).\n113|8. Negative/refusal cases — every gate above, each with a narrowing\n114|   mutant killed by a named behavioral test (§3).\n115|\n116|0 of 8 rows delivered as a public CLI surface: stated bound, not a gap\n117|in assigned shared behavior. No unsupported capability advertised.\n118|\n119|## 5. Reviewer-addendum evidence (observed this run, scratch probe deleted after)\n120|\n121|A temporary in-package probe (created, run, deleted in this run; not\n122|in the candidate) recorded actual production behavior; full log\n123|attached as `TASK-260830-21gygk_revalidation-probe-ffb76b.log`:\n124|\n125|- P1: bare-NAME plan won at a peer tier (source hostA, session …90ac).\n126|  After local gained the same live name, fresh `Resolve(\"beta\")`\n127|  moved to the local copy (…90ad, peer `\"\"`) — the resolution-drift\n128|  premise holds — while `Revalidate(plan)` returned nil.\n129|- P2: bare-`id:` plan on one copy; after another allowed source gained\n130|  a disagreeing record copy, fresh `Resolve` refused\n131|  `integrity_failure: … disagreeing record digests across sources`,\n132|  while `Revalidate(plan)` returned nil.\n133|- P3 control: appending an event to the plan-source chain made\n134|  `Revalidate` return `selector_plan_stale` — revalidation watches\n135|  the plan source, so the P1/P2 nils are scope, not blindness.\n136|\n137|Normative comparison (SPEC.v0.6.0.md): the plan binds one provenance\n138|source (`source_host_id`: \"for a bare union match, provenance host of\n139|the selected entry\", l11948) and one complete validated read of that\n140|source (`source_index_digest`: \"Digest of the complete validated\n141|index read used for selection\", l11950; completeness contrasts with\n142|partial/cached reads per §14.7.1, no union-digest construction is\n143|defined anywhere). Revalidation compares every bound fact; the\n144|invalidation list (l11967–11971) names bound-member changes only, and\n145|\"An unrelated index change may conservatively require a fresh plan\"\n146|(l11973–11974) is permissive. Detecting name-tier drift inside\n147|`Revalidate` would be re-resolving by name, which the spec forbids\n148|(l11972); the plan pins the UUID, and invocation drift is owned by\n149|the caller-side composed binding (`SEL-CASE-…-session/source-mismatch`\n150|witnesses: \"Plan/current agreement alone authorizes nothing\",\n151|l12122–12125; receiver validates \"against its independently read\n152|exact session, winning lease, complete authority\", l12049–12052).\n153|All revalidation members stay `endpoint-local … never cross-compared`\n154|(l12127–12128, l12143–12152). No corrective product change follows\n155|from this comparison; the ruling is the reviewer's.\n156|\n157|- `lease_record_id`: reported as a declared delta, not equivalence.\n158|  The 16-member table requires it (l11952); this stack contains no\n159|  Lease Record objects, so there is no validated digest to bind and\n160|  the wire format carries no such field (a future member without a\n161|  disposition row fails the publication gate closed, l12130–12133).\n162|  The winning lease triple (epoch/lease-ID/owner) binds from the\n163|  validated envelope derivation, satisfying its own row (l11953).\n164|  CLI 5 attach `lease_record_id` admission is caller/receiver-leaf\n165|  owned. Fabricating a digest would be an unsupported claim.\n166|- §14.7.3: shared-library scope delivered is authoritative\n167|  read-model summaries with derived facts only and whole-read refusal\n168|  (row 4/5); wire CLI Result 5 / public-document refusal is\n169|  caller-leaf owned.\n170|\n171|## 6. Stated bounds (unchanged)\n172|\n173|`authority_heads` binds validated event-head digests of the plan\n174|source only; union precedence facts are not re-checked (§5 evidence).\n175|Wire exit codes, §14.7.3 public-document list refusal, §14.7.4\n176|recovery, effect authorization, and composed invocation-to-plan\n177|bindings are caller-leaf owned; `BoundariesFor` names every boundary\n178|callers must revalidate at. Plans authorize read projection only.\n179|Reads across calls are not an atomic snapshot; transports, peer\n180|authentication, freshness, host metadata, and observation contracts\n181|remain upstream caller inputs.\n182|\n183|Ready for review (producer handoff; independent Astra review and\n184|orchestrator integration own the remaining path).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
