{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4dd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":201,"recorded_at":1780531400000397,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0886b-4439-7223-9ec4-95542b82e20f"},"task_id":"01a0886b-4439-7223-9ec4-95542b82e20f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0886b-4439-7223-9ec4-95542b82e20f","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rework.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk results (rework after CR rev2 review)\n2|\n3|Scope: v0.6.0 selector contract (\\u00a7\\u00a714.7/14.7.1, shared SelectionPlan\n4|construction/revalidation \\u00a714.7.2, refining \\u00a72.3, authoritative summaries\n5|\\u00a7\\u00a75.7/14.7.3). Authority: spec v0.6.0 commit\n6|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6` (STORY-260908-18woqo landed).\n7|Branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns` at\n8|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`, descending from\n9|`origin/main` `8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`. Candidate left\n10|UNCOMMITTED in the managed Story worktree for the handoff snapshot:\n11|tracked delta `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`,\n12|`internal/sessrepo/store.go`, `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go`\n13|(predecessor bytes preserved); untracked `internal/sessquery/`\n14|(16 files: 6 implementation, 8 tests, TRACEABILITY, mutate battery).\n15|No `ax` session surface exists in this tree; CLI delivery, wire exits,\n16|lifecycle effects, and the \\u00a714.7.4 recovery flow are caller/recovery-leaf\n17|owned. Independent Astra medium review and orchestrator integration own\n18|the remaining path.\n19|\n20|## 1. Rev2 findings disposition (all four addressed in the shared layer)\n21|\n22|- FINDING 1 \\u2014 revalidation ignored conflicting authority outside the\n23|  selected source. `Revalidate` and `bindPlan` now run\n24|  `validateAuthorityUnion` (`internal/sessquery/revalidate.go`) over\n25|  the local and every allowlisted source for the pinned UUID after the\n26|  plan-source checks: a disagreeing non-parked record digest is\n27|  `integrity_failure` (same class/message as `Resolve`); a\n28|  contradictory observed winning lease or fresh tombstone evidence is\n29|  `selector_plan_stale`; zero-lease copies skip only the lease check;\n30|  parked copies and absences never contradict; unreadable required\n31|  sources keep their read-failure class. Names are never re-resolved\n32|  and no selection is substituted: a same-name gain for another UUID\n33|  stays current, an agreeing replica stays current, and\n34|  explicit-source no-fallback is preserved. Reviewer probe\n35|  `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse` carried verbatim into\n36|  `review_test.go` and green, plus seven new union tests.\n37|- FINDING 2 \\u2014 16-member plan with lease authority. `SelectionPlan`\n38|  gains `lease_record_id` (struct, wire, canonical digest, shapes).\n39|  This stack persists no standalone `urn:ax:schema:lease` objects\n40|  (sessrepo stores Session Records and Session Events only), so the\n41|  member binds the locally attested canonical digest of the validated\n42|  winning envelope lease, recomputed from validated facts on every\n43|  build and revalidation \\u2014 stated exactly in `plan.go`, TRACEABILITY\n44|  bounds, and README, never a fabricated object digest. Record-only\n45|  builds refuse `selector_bootstrap_incomplete`; local builds without\n46|  a known local host refuse `invalid_config`; shapes require a bound\n47|  source UUIDv7, the lease attestation digest, and the full positive\n48|  triple. The plan-source path recompares the attestation, closing\n49|  hand-built digest forgery. `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord`\n50|  carried verbatim and green.\n51|- FINDING 3 \\u2014 authoritative summary refusal. `List`/`Status` refuse\n52|  record-only bootstraps with `selector_bootstrap_incomplete`, whole\n53|  list on any unrepresentable record (mixed listings included, nil\n54|  rows, nothing omitted); `InspectLocal` keeps raw\n55|  recovery-diagnostics access by design and is not a public summary\n56|  entry. New closed `AuthoritativeStatus`/`AuthoritativeList`\n57|  (`summary.go`) bind owner names only from validated host metadata,\n58|  roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from\n59|  validated observations, and pass optional liveness/capability/\n60|  workspace observations through only when supplied; missing required\n61|  facts refuse `selector_observation_unavailable` and nothing is\n62|  inferred. `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse` carried verbatim\n63|  and green, plus eight new summary tests.\n64|- FINDING 4 \\u2014 narrowing evidence. All seven `&& false` clause-disables\n65|  replaced with single-member admissions (revocation/hostA,\n66|  config/hostC-ws, binding/hostB-ws, index/idB, parked chain-mismatch\n67|  record, leaseB triple+attestation, two-event chain), plus new\n68|  narrowings for both cross-copy agreement call sites, union\n69|  record/lease/tombstone, plan bootstrap/host, summary bootstrap, and\n70|  observation host: 33 narrowing + 3 ordering mutants, every one\n71|  KILLED by a named behavioral test through the delivered harness\n72|  (battery exit 0; CONTROL/NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE\n73|  distinct, never kills). Notable diagnosis: the \"record replacement\"\n74|  fixture presents as a parked chain-mismatch with an empty digest,\n75|  not a renamed live record \\u2014 the first N-rev-record plant (admitting\n76|  name \"renamed\") SURVIVED and exposed it; the corrected plant admits\n77|  the parked mismatch and is killed with degradation to the lease\n78|  reason. TRACEABILITY claims corrected (no \"8 of 8 in full\", no\n79|  \"every bound fact\", per-gate mutant rows).\n80|\n81|## 2. Validation re-derived on the final candidate (real exits)\n82|\n83|| Command | Exit |\n84|| --- | --- |\n85|| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n86|| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n87|| `gofmt -l internal/` (empty) | 0 |\n88|| `git diff --check -- internal/ LOGBOOK.md README.md` | 0 |\n89|| `go test ./... -count=1` (all 26 packages ok) | 0 |\n90|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` (90.9% / 87.6% / 92.2%) | 0 |\n91|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -race -count=1` | 0 |\n92|| tracked-JSON gate (`git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c ...`) | 0 |\n93|| mutant battery `python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` (33 N + 3 B KILLED, 0 survivors) | 0 |\n94|\n95|Raw logs: `TASK-260830-21gygk_validation-rework.log`,\n96|`TASK-260830-21gygk_mutants-rework.json` (attached); per-mutant logs\n97|in worktree scratch `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/mutants-rework/logs/`.\n98|\n99|## 3. Acceptance: 8 of 8 AC rows driven at the shared library boundary\n100|\n101|Per `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md` (production call site +\n102|named tests per row): bare UUID/name selectors, qualified selectors,\n103|ambiguity, list summaries, status summaries, stable deterministic\n104|sorting, SelectionPlan build/revalidate, negative/refusal cases. 0 of\n105|8 rows delivered as a public CLI surface: stated caller-integration\n106|bound, not a gap in assigned shared behavior. No unsupported\n107|capability advertised.\n108|\n109|Ready for review (producer handoff; independent Astra review and\n110|orchestrator integration own the remaining path).","final_result":true}}}
