{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":203,"recorded_at":1780531400000401,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0886b-441a-7fd3-a0f0-33328c8f8cf8"},"task_id":"01a0886b-441a-7fd3-a0f0-33328c8f8cf8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0886b-441a-7fd3-a0f0-33328c8f8cf8","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — rev3 review: changes requested\n2|\n3|Immutable CR-TASK-260830-21gygk-3 revision 3; tree\n4|`ad077090f354e633a6a7a3eed48ef35dc60c0ad4`, base\n5|`8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint\n6|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`.\n7|Authority: candidate internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md, pinned spec commit\n8|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. This reviews the assigned shared\n9|library, with CLI invocation/envelopes and durable recovery left to their owners.\n10|\n11|## Findings requiring rework\n12|\n13|### 1. P1 — Required Lease Record identity is still replaced with another object\n14|\n15|`internal/sessquery/digest.go:136` fingerprints only session_id, lease_epoch,\n16|lease_id and owner_host_id. `plan.go:266` binds that result as LeaseRecordID;\n17|`revalidate.go:105` verifies the same substitute. No actual Lease Record is\n18|read or admitted by these production paths. SPEC 14.7.2:11953 requires the\n19|validated winning Lease Record digest, with all lease facts from that same\n20|record; 5.3 defines its closed schema and identity. A four-field observation\n21|is a different object, even when all four values agree. Calling it locally\n22|attested does not make it that Lease Record.\n23|\n24|Reviewer production probes, both FAIL (test command exit 1):\n25|- `TestRev3RealLeaseRecordIdentity`: constructs a real epoch-1 create Lease\n26|  Record, validates it through `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity`, then\n27|  drives `Reader.BuildPlan`. Expected actual record digest starts `28730fb6`;\n28|  returned envelope-observation digest starts `5f6f848f`. Full values and\n29|  validated record bytes are in regression.log.\n30|- `TestRev3DifferentAttestationMustNotAuthorize`: BuildPlan → Marshal →\n31|  ParsePlan → Revalidate accepts the different observation attestation with\n32|  no Lease Record ever provided.\n33|\n34|Exact probe bound: the candidate exposes **no supported Lease Record input**\n35|on Reader/Repository. The real validated fixture is an independent identity\n36|oracle, not a claim to have supplied it through an invented storage path.\n37|This absent integration is itself the remaining requirement. Add real shared\n38|Lease Record acquisition/admission, bind its canonical identity and validated\n39|heads, and test same-record facts, changed/missing record and substitution.\n40|Do not relabel an envelope digest or defer this shared requirement to CLI.\n41|The added nonempty source host and positive tuple checks are useful fixes;\n42|the old field-presence reviewer test is insufficient for semantic identity.\n43|\n44|### 2. P1 — The authoritative summary still succeeds without required facts\n45|\n46|`summary.go:50-90,239-241` treats unknown process/workspace/capability\n47|observations as successful nil fields. It exposes WorkspacePresent rather\n48|than the required workspace_status, and a string slice rather than validated\n49|CapabilitySummary values. `summary.go:38` also admits host names up to 128\n50|characters. SPEC 14.7.3:12348-12372 preserves the closed summary shape and\n51|requires unavailable required observations to refuse. The inherited table at\n52|11423 requires owner_host_name[1..64], workspace_status, capability summaries\n53|and warnings; status at 11437 requires a boolean process_present.\n54|\n55|`TestRev3UnknownRequiredObservationsRefuse` fails for both\n56|Reader.AuthoritativeStatus and Reader.AuthoritativeList: an empty observation\n57|map returns successful output instead of selector_observation_unavailable.\n58|`TestRev3HostNameBound64` fails because a 65-character host name succeeds.\n59|The diagnostic JSON records these missing facts; JSON member casing itself\n60|is NOT a finding because wire serialization is caller-owned.\n61|\n62|Connect the shared authoritative layer to the required validated observation\n63|facts, distinguish unknown from established absence (including a legitimately\n64|empty capability map), enforce the actual bounds, and refuse the whole list\n65|when a required row is unrepresentable. Caller-owned formatting cannot recover\n66|missing semantics without reimplementing this layer. Owner/lease facts also\n67|need the actual Lease Record integration in finding 1. New bootstrap,\n68|mixed-list, host-metadata and checkpoint-timestamp refusals do work; preserve\n69|them and the diagnostic low-level projector.\n70|\n71|### 3. P1 — Copy equality is not complete authority union/winner derivation\n72|\n73|`revalidate.go:201-233` compares every nonzero copy's lease for equality with\n74|the selected source. `bindPlan` calls it for a new plan as well. A known older\n75|lease is not a contradictory winning lease: SPEC 5.3 selects the greatest\n76|(epoch, lease_id) in the union and preserves losing histories. 14.7.2 requires\n77|that winner, current tombstones and the complete authority union.\n78|\n79|`TestRev3BuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy` drives production repository event entry\n80|points and then fresh `BuildPlan(\"beta@local\")`: local has epoch 2, peer has\n81|the same immutable record at epoch 1. BuildPlan returns selector_plan_stale\n82|although no prior plan exists and the union has a deterministic epoch-2 winner.\n83|The test FAILS. Bound: these are the candidate's supported event-chain facts,\n84|not proof of actual Lease Record storage (finding 1). It exposes that equality\n85|alone cannot implement the required union even within that supported model.\n86|\n87|Derive and validate the actual union/winner, while retaining exact selected\n88|source provenance and never re-resolving by name. Bind all lease/event/tombstone\n89|heads used in the decision; current code stores only the selected event tail.\n90|Also audit the unconditional parked-copy skip at revalidate.go:206: failed\n91|observations cannot establish a complete authority read. I did not rerun a\n92|separate parked-copy regression; do not count that audit question as another\n93|measured failure. Preserve the new same-UUID record-conflict refusal and\n94|read-failure classes, which pass. Different-UUID same-name gain is still not\n95|itself a defect or a reason to retarget the plan.\n96|\n97|## Negative evidence and claim corrections\n98|\n99|The same delivered run()/classifier was independently executed on three\n100|isolated plants against the candidate's unmodified behavioral suites:\n101|\n102|| Plant | Result | Exit | Meaning |\n103|| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n104|| Harmless applied comment | SURVIVED | 0 | Actual same-instrument survivor control |\n105|| N-record-nonempty | SURVIVED | 0 | Admit a changed nonempty record digest for idA at the selected-source comparison; parked/empty records still refuse |\n106|| N-observation-host | KILLED | 1 | TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses fails for one owner's missing metadata |\n107|\n108|The shipped N-rev-record now narrows the gate but exercises a parked empty\n109|record and fails on a later refusal reason. That proves the tested error\n110|ordering for that case; it does not establish behavior for a validated changed\n111|record. The new survivor is a coverage gap at this comparison, **not proof of\n112|an end-to-end unauthorized acceptance**: later heads/index checks may subsume\n113|it. Add a meaningful changed-record witness or document and test exact\n114|subsumption, rather than calling all record cases covered.\n115|\n116|The producer manifest actually contains **35 N + 3 B = 38 KILLED**, not the\n117|33 N + 3 B described in its resource description/outcome. Its other results\n118|are CONTROL x2, NOT_APPLIED x1, COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE x1; none is SURVIVED.\n119|I located 41 raw logs (the NOT_APPLIED plant has none), checked named failures\n120|against every manifest entry, and preserved those logs in this bundle. They\n121|match. The original mutation source copy is absent at the inspected run path;\n122|therefore exact source attribution of all old plants is not independently\n123|established by a retained copy. I did not rerun the full battery or convert\n124|that absence into a failing behavioral result. Fresh three-plant evidence is\n125|exact-candidate-bound. Correct counts and “all four addressed”, “8/8 complete”\n126|and actual-Lease-equivalence claims in outcome/README/TRACEABILITY after fixes.\n127|\n128|## AC coverage ratio\n129|\n130|**8 of 8 AC rows driven through shared production entries; 4 of 8 established\n131|within the supplied-repository boundary; 4 of 8 partial/failing.** This uses the\n132|existing eight-row AC decomposition, not a claim to enumerate all normative\n133|fixture clauses. **0 of 8 public CLI rows delivered** remains an explicitly\n134|accepted caller-integration bound, not a rejection reason.\n135|\n136|| Row | Production call site and named candidate tests | Result |\n137|| --- | --- | --- |\n138|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established within supplied config/repository boundary |\n139|| Qualified selectors | Reader.Resolve → resolveExplicit; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established |\n140|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve → matchName/checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established for resolution; plans separately below |\n141|| List summaries | Reader.List/AuthoritativeList; TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals, TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole, TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse | Partial: finding 2, plus actual lease authority |\n142|| Status summaries | Reader.AuthoritativeStatus; TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses, TestAuthoritativeCheckpointRequiresTimestamp; reviewer observation/name tests | Partial: findings 1–2 |\n143|| Deterministic sorting | Reader.List/Resolve; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Established |\n144|| SelectionPlan | Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan; TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse; reviewer lease/lagging-copy probes | Partial: findings 1 and 3 |\n145|| Negative/refusal | Reader.Resolve/List/Status/BuildPlan/Revalidate; candidate refusal suites and reviewer mutation/probe logs | Partial: missing semantic admission/refusal evidence above |\n146|\n147|## Validation and preservation\n148|\n149|- Exported exact tree using git archive to task scratch. All 42 candidate paths\n150|  match live worktree bytes (candidate-manifest.json). No product, branch,\n151|  index or board checkout file edited. No stray --help tree or .task-board path\n152|  in the immutable delta. HEAD remains the supplied Story checkpoint;\n153|  `git rev-list --count HEAD..main` was 0, not used as a substitute for tree identity.\n154|- Independently reran `go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -v`\n155|  on the exact archive: **exit 0**. Full log attached. Target is Go on\n156|  darwin/arm64, Go 1.25.5; no iOS target exists for this library work.\n157|- Reviewer-only probes in archive: `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev3' -count=1 -v`:\n158|  **exit 1**, five failed top-level tests (six failing assertions/subcases),\n159|  one diagnostic PASS. Source and full log attached, then probe source removed\n160|  from archive; live candidate never modified.\n161|- Fresh three-plant driver **exit 0** means evidence collection succeeded,\n162|  not that all plants were killed. Per-plant exits above. Runner restores bytes.\n163|- `git diff --check BASE TREE`: **exit 0**. Reused attached producer\n164|  validation-rework.log for full tests, coverage, race, build, vet, gofmt and\n165|  JSON gate (all report exit=0); did not independently rerun those full gates.\n166|  Actual rev3 publication validation resource has five `[exit 0]` markers.\n167|  These green results do not override reviewer failures.\n168|- Read full prior rev2 verdict and its evidence archive inventory, current\n169|  rework outcome, mutation manifest and validation resources. No need to reopen\n170|  settled predecessor crash/reducer/canonical reviews. provhost and sessstate\n171|  match checkpoint; the only predecessor production delta is store.go's exact\n172|  case-sensitive name match and its regression, covered by the package rerun.\n173|- Missing Story skill symlinks were handled by reading the existing\n174|  Curator-managed Go skill from main; no install or infrastructure edits.\n175|\n176|## Disposition / task logbook\n177|\n178|**Changes requested; route TASK-260830-21gygk (implement-name-resolution-and-summary)\n179|to to-dev.** This is implementable shared-layer rework, not blocked on a new\n180|human product decision. Preserve full assigned scope. This outcome records\n181|review findings in the task logbook; product LOGBOOK remains read-only.\n182|No accept_cr, commit, checkpoint, integration or landing performed.","final_result":true}}}
