{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":205,"recorded_at":1780531400000405,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0886b-43f5-7080-8c1e-0649824ae665"},"task_id":"01a0886b-43f5-7080-8c1e-0649824ae665","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0886b-43f5-7080-8c1e-0649824ae665","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — revision 2 review: changes requested\n2|\n3|Reviewed immutable CR-TASK-260830-21gygk-2 revision 2, candidate tree\n4|`fbff1e0a9f443b1378f04dd108a93c07449ba551`, base\n5|`8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint\n6|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`.\n7|Authority is the candidate's pinned SPEC.v0.6.0.md, spec commit: `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`.\n8|Reviewed assigned shared-library scope, not future CLI invocation ownership.\n9|\n10|## Blocking findings\n11|\n12|1. **P1 — Revalidation ignores conflicting current authority outside the selected source.**\n13|   `internal/sessquery/revalidate.go:62-123` reads only the plan-source repository;\n14|   `plan.go:229-286` binds only its event tail. SPEC 14.7.2 lines 11965-11974\n15|   requires the same immutable record, current tombstones, complete authority\n16|   union and winning lease to be validated before proceeding. In\n17|   `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse`, BuildPlan selects a peer's\n18|   UUID, then another allowed source (local) gains a different immutable\n19|   record for that same UUID. Fresh Resolve refuses integrity_failure;\n20|   Revalidate(oldPlan) incorrectly returns nil. The probe fails, exit 1.\n21|   This is an exact-UUID authority check, not forbidden name re-resolution.\n22|   Bind and revalidate the required complete authority, with class-preserving\n23|   read/integrity refusals and changed-head/winner tests across sources.\n24|   Keep explicit-source selection/no-fallback semantics intact.\n25|   P1 in the producer's diagnostic (a different UUID gains the old name\n26|   locally) alone does NOT prove a defect: no silent retargeting is allowed,\n27|   and unrelated index invalidation is permissive. I do not require rerunning\n28|   name resolution or treating every such gain as stale. Producer P2 does\n29|   establish a different issue: contradictory authority for the pinned UUID.\n30|\n31|2. **P1 — SelectionPlan does not implement the required plan members and lease authority.**\n32|   `internal/sessquery/plan.go:122-165,249-266` and\n33|   `revalidate.go:204-218,245-264` omit lease_record_id, permit empty source host,\n34|   and accept the all-empty/zero lease tuple. SPEC 14.7.2 lines 11939-11959\n35|   requires the exact 16-member plan, a source UUIDv7, a validated winning Lease\n36|   Record digest, and positive epoch/UUID lease-owner facts from that same record.\n37|   `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord` drives BuildPlan and Marshal and fails\n38|   because lease_record_id is absent. Committed candidate tests\n39|   TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts and TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionBindsEmptyLease\n40|   explicitly protect empty host/lease behavior. A missing Lease Record owner\n41|   is a dependency gap, not equivalent authority or a scope exemption. Connect\n42|   the shared builder/revalidator to validated lease facts; refuse unavailable\n43|   required facts rather than returning a conforming-looking partial plan.\n44|   Do not fabricate a digest. Action-specific invocation binding remains caller\n45|   owned, but the required shared plan field does not.\n46|\n47|3. **P1 — Assigned authoritative summary refusal is missing.**\n48|   `internal/sessquery/query.go:94-155` exposes only an internal projection.\n49|   `Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` succeed for record-only bootstrap with\n50|   epoch 0/empty owner. Both subtests of TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse\n51|   fail through these production entries. SPEC 14.7.3 lines 12354-12372 requires\n52|   selector_bootstrap_incomplete for a complete record-only authority read,\n53|   selector_observation_unavailable for unavailable required observations/host\n54|   metadata, and whole-list refusal for an unrepresentable record. No shared\n55|   summary API implements those classifications or accepts the needed validated\n56|   observation facts. Preserving the accepted low-level projector is fine;\n57|   it does not deliver the assigned authoritative summary layer. Add that layer\n58|   and named negative tests, including a mixed healthy/incomplete list and\n59|   unavailable host/observation facts. CLI envelope/exit rendering and the\n60|   durable bootstrap recovery operation remain their existing caller owners.\n61|   The current cliresult shape-rejection test does not prove these refusals.\n62|\n63|4. **P2 — Narrowing evidence and completion claims overstate coverage.**\n64|   `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py:81-87` uses `&& false` for revocation,\n65|   configuration, source binding, index, record, lease and heads comparisons.\n66|   These are full clause disables, even though named N-*; preserving the text\n67|   does not preserve the gate. Several only change a later refusal's reason.\n68|   Cross-copy agreement is explicitly listed without a weakening in\n69|   TRACEABILITY.md. Replace/supplement these with genuine single-class-member\n70|   admission mutants and named behavioral failures, covering each required\n71|   gate including the fixes above. Correct TRACEABILITY.md's “8 of 8 ... in\n72|   full”, “every bound fact”, and “each killed by narrowing” claims and the\n73|   corresponding README/outcome claims. Existing byte-equal mutant sources and\n74|   raw logs support 29 behavioral KILLED results, not 26 qualifying narrowing\n75|   proofs. Controls are correctly separate: CONTROL x2, NOT_APPLIED x1,\n76|   COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE x1. None is a SURVIVED measurement.\n77|   I independently used the same run()/classifier with a harmless comment\n78|   plant: SURVIVED exit 0. A true one-session index-gate narrowing was KILLED\n79|   exit 1 by TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange/unrelated_session_change_changes_index.\n80|   Thus the classifier works; the shipped battery's evidence coverage needs repair.\n81|\n82|## AC coverage ratio and bounds\n83|\n84|**8 of 8 producer AC rows are exercised at some shared-library production entry;\n85|4 of 8 are established within the supplied-repository test boundary; 4 of 8\n86|remain partial or failing.** Exercised is not implemented in full. This is the\n87|producer's eight-row breakdown of the assigned AC, not a claim to enumerate\n88|all normative fixture rows. **0 of 8 public CLI rows delivered** is an explicit\n89|caller integration bound and is not itself a rejection reason.\n90|\n91|| Row | Production entry / named candidate tests | Review result |\n92|| --- | --- | --- |\n93|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established for supplied repository/config inputs |\n94|| Qualified | Reader.Resolve; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established for supplied inputs; does not attest live peer transport/config acquisition |\n95|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve → matchName/checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Resolution tests established; current-plan authority remains finding 1 |\n96|| List summaries | Reader.List; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure | Partial: finding 3 |\n97|| Status summaries | Reader.Status/InspectLocal; TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult and qualified status tests | Partial: finding 3 |\n98|| Deterministic order | Reader.List/Resolve; TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established within supplied-input boundary |\n99|| Plan | Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan; TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts, TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestPlanDigestAndMarshalRoundTrip | Partial: findings 1–2 |\n100|| Negative/refusal | Reader.Resolve/List/Status/BuildPlan/Revalidate; named refusal tests and mutation battery | Partial: findings 1–4 |\n101|\n102|Freshness/transport authentication are not proven by local learned repository\n103|handles, as SPEC 14.7.1 expressly says. Current tests must not be cited as such\n104|proof. Shared APIs should expose the required validated facts/refusals without\n105|requiring callers to implement another resolver.\n106|\n107|## Verification and preservation\n108|\n109|- Exported the exact immutable tree to task scratch with git archive. All 38\n110|  changed paths matched both archive and live worktree bytes after review;\n111|  candidate-manifest.json records SHA-256 values. No product or branch edit.\n112|- Independently ran `go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -v`\n113|  on that archive before probes: exit 0. Raw review-tests.log attached in bundle.\n114|- Added reviewer-only regression tests to the scratch archive, ran\n115|  `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestReviewer' -count=1 -v`: exit 1,\n116|  three failed top-level tests (four failed assertions/subcases). Saved their\n117|  source and log, then removed them from the archive; no candidate test changed.\n118|- Independent classifier/narrowing check: driver exit 0, SURVIVED plant exit 0,\n119|  KILLED narrowing exit 1, full named behavioral tests recorded. This is a\n120|  two-plant check, not a rerun of the producer's whole battery.\n121|- Reused attached ffb76b evidence for build, vet, formatting, full suite,\n122|  coverage (91.0% query / 87.6% repo / 92.2% state), race and JSON validation;\n123|  these report exit 0. I did not rerun those full gates. Read the actual rev2\n124|  CR validation resource: recorded command exit markers are 0; board validation\n125|  warning counts are not product acceptance. No failing reviewer probe is\n126|  converted into green by that earlier log.\n127|- Retained predecessor provhost/sessstate bytes match checkpoint exactly.\n128|  Only predecessor repo code change is exact-case name matching at store.go:135\n129|  plus its test, consistent with the normative exact-name rule. Narrow tests\n130|  passed. No reason to reopen settled crash/reducer/canonical admission reviews.\n131|- LOGBOOK replay preserves predecessor and new-leaf entries; no stray --help\n132|  tree or board checkout path is in the 38-path CR delta. The adopted spec pin\n133|  and catalog remain at the supplied base, not replaced with historical v0.5.\n134|- Failed skill-path probe: this Story worktree has no .codex/skills or\n135|  .agents/bin. Read the existing Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill from\n136|  the main checkout; no installation or shared-infra modification performed.\n137|\n138|## Disposition\n139|\n140|Changes requested; route TASK-260830-21gygk (implement-name-resolution-and-summary)\n141|to **to-dev**, not blocked. This is implementable rework/dependency integration,\n142|not a new product decision. Preserve full assigned scope. No accept_cr,\n143|commit, checkpoint, branch switch, or landing performed. The reviewer logbook\n144|entry is this durable task outcome; product LOGBOOK is left read-only.","final_result":true}}}
