{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":207,"recorded_at":1780531400000409,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b40257f539f156efafb59858b","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — revision 2 review: changes requested\n2|\n3|Reviewed immutable CR-TASK-260830-21gygk-2 revision 2, candidate tree\n4|`fbff1e0a9f443b1378f04dd108a93c07449ba551`, base\n5|`8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint\n6|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`.\n7|Authority is the candidate's pinned SPEC.v0.6.0.md, spec commit: `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`.\n8|Reviewed assigned shared-library scope, not future CLI invocation ownership.\n9|\n10|## Blocking findings\n11|\n12|1. **P1 — Revalidation ignores conflicting current authority outside the selected source.**\n13|   `internal/sessquery/revalidate.go:62-123` reads only the plan-source repository;\n14|   `plan.go:229-286` binds only its event tail. SPEC 14.7.2 lines 11965-11974\n15|   requires the same immutable record, current tombstones, complete authority\n16|   union and winning lease to be validated before proceeding. In\n17|   `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse`, BuildPlan selects a peer's\n18|   UUID, then another allowed source (local) gains a different immutable\n19|   record for that same UUID. Fresh Resolve refuses integrity_failure;\n20|   Revalidate(oldPlan) incorrectly returns nil. The probe fails, exit 1.\n21|   This is an exact-UUID authority check, not forbidden name re-resolution.\n22|   Bind and revalidate the required complete authority, with class-preserving\n23|   read/integrity refusals and changed-head/winner tests across sources.\n24|   Keep explicit-source selection/no-fallback semantics intact.\n25|   P1 in the producer's diagnostic (a different UUID gains the old name\n26|   locally) alone does NOT prove a defect: no silent retargeting is allowed,\n27|   and unrelated index invalidation is permissive. I do not require rerunning\n28|   name resolution or treating every such gain as stale. Producer P2 does\n29|   establish a different issue: contradictory authority for the pinned UUID.\n30|\n31|2. **P1 — SelectionPlan does not implement the required plan members and lease authority.**\n32|   `internal/sessquery/plan.go:122-165,249-266` and\n33|   `revalidate.go:204-218,245-264` omit lease_record_id, permit empty source host,\n34|   and accept the all-empty/zero lease tuple. SPEC 14.7.2 lines 11939-11959\n35|   requires the exact 16-member plan, a source UUIDv7, a validated winning Lease\n36|   Record digest, and positive epoch/UUID lease-owner facts from that same record.\n37|   `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord` drives BuildPlan and Marshal and fails\n38|   because lease_record_id is absent. Committed candidate tests\n39|   TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts and TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionBindsEmptyLease\n40|   explicitly protect empty host/lease behavior. A missing Lease Record owner\n41|   is a dependency gap, not equivalent authority or a scope exemption. Connect\n42|   the shared builder/revalidator to validated lease facts; refuse unavailable\n43|   required facts rather than returning a conforming-looking partial plan.\n44|   Do not fabricate a digest. Action-specific invocation binding remains caller\n45|   owned, but the required shared plan field does not.\n46|\n47|3. **P1 — Assigned authoritative summary refusal is missing.**\n48|   `internal/sessquery/query.go:94-155` exposes only an internal projection.\n49|   `Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` succeed for record-only bootstrap with\n50|   epoch 0/empty owner. Both subtests of TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse\n51|   fail through these production entries. SPEC 14.7.3 lines 12354-12372 requires\n52|   selector_bootstrap_incomplete for a complete record-only authority read,\n53|   selector_observation_unavailable for unavailable required observations/host\n54|   metadata, and whole-list refusal for an unrepresentable record. No shared\n55|   summary API implements those classifications or accepts the needed validated\n56|   observation facts. Preserving the accepted low-level projector is fine;\n57|   it does not deliver the assigned authoritative summary layer. Add that layer\n58|   and named negative tests, including a mixed healthy/incomplete list and\n59|   unavailable host/observation facts. CLI envelope/exit rendering and the\n60|   durable bootstrap recovery operation remain their existing caller owners.\n61|   The current cliresult shape-rejection test does not prove these refusals.\n62|\n63|4. **P2 — Narrowing evidence and completion claims overstate coverage.**\n64|   `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py:81-87` uses `&& false` for revocation,\n65|   configuration, source binding, index, record, lease and heads comparisons.\n66|   These are full clause disables, even though named N-*; preserving the text\n67|   does not preserve the gate. Several only change a later refusal's reason.\n68|   Cross-copy agreement is explicitly listed without a weakening in\n69|   TRACEABILITY.md. Replace/supplement these with genuine single-class-member\n70|   admission mutants and named behavioral failures, covering each required\n71|   gate including the fixes above. Correct TRACEABILITY.md's “8 of 8 ... in\n72|   full”, “every bound fact”, and “each killed by narrowing” claims and the\n73|   corresponding README/outcome claims. Existing byte-equal mutant sources and\n74|   raw logs support 29 behavioral KILLED results, not 26 qualifying narrowing\n75|   proofs. Controls are correctly separate: CONTROL x2, NOT_APPLIED x1,\n76|   COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE x1. None is a SURVIVED measurement.\n77|   I independently used the same run()/classifier with a harmless comment\n78|   plant: SURVIVED exit 0. A true one-session index-gate narrowing was KILLED\n79|   exit 1 by TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange/unrelated_session_change_changes_index.\n80|   Thus the classifier works; the shipped battery's evidence coverage needs repair.\n81|\n82|## AC coverage ratio and bounds\n83|\n84|**8 of 8 producer AC rows are exercised at some shared-library production entry;\n85|4 of 8 are established within the supplied-repository test boundary; 4 of 8\n86|remain partial or failing.** Exercised is not implemented in full. This is the\n87|producer's eight-row breakdown of the assigned AC, not a claim to enumerate\n88|all normative fixture rows. **0 of 8 public CLI rows delivered** is an explicit\n89|caller integration bound and is not itself a rejection reason.\n90|\n91|| Row | Production entry / named candidate tests | Review result |\n92|| --- | --- | --- |\n93|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established for supplied repository/config inputs |\n94|| Qualified | Reader.Resolve; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established for supplied inputs; does not attest live peer transport/config acquisition |\n95|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve → matchName/checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Resolution tests established; current-plan authority remains finding 1 |\n96|| List summaries | Reader.List; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure | Partial: finding 3 |\n97|| Status summaries | Reader.Status/InspectLocal; TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult and qualified status tests | Partial: finding 3 |\n98|| Deterministic order | Reader.List/Resolve; TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established within supplied-input boundary |\n99|| Plan | Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan; TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts, TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestPlanDigestAndMarshalRoundTrip | Partial: findings 1–2 |\n100|| Negative/refusal | Reader.Resolve/List/Status/BuildPlan/Revalidate; named refusal tests and mutation battery | Partial: findings 1–4 |\n101|\n102|Freshness/transport authentication are not proven by local learned repository\n103|handles, as SPEC 14.7.1 expressly says. Current tests must not be cited as such\n104|proof. Shared APIs should expose the required validated facts/refusals without\n105|requiring callers to implement another resolver.\n106|\n107|## Verification and preservation\n108|\n109|- Exported the exact immutable tree to task scratch with git archive. All 38\n110|  changed paths matched both archive and live worktree bytes after review;\n111|  candidate-manifest.json records SHA-256 values. No product or branch edit.\n112|- Independently ran `go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -v`\n113|  on that archive before probes: exit 0. Raw review-tests.log attached in bundle.\n114|- Added reviewer-only regression tests to the scratch archive, ran\n115|  `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestReviewer' -count=1 -v`: exit 1,\n116|  three failed top-level tests (four failed assertions/subcases). Saved their\n117|  source and log, then removed them from the archive; no candidate test changed.\n118|- Independent classifier/narrowing check: driver exit 0, SURVIVED plant exit 0,\n119|  KILLED narrowing exit 1, full named behavioral tests recorded. This is a\n120|  two-plant check, not a rerun of the producer's whole battery.\n121|- Reused attached ffb76b evidence for build, vet, formatting, full suite,\n122|  coverage (91.0% query / 87.6% repo / 92.2% state), race and JSON validation;\n123|  these report exit 0. I did not rerun those full gates. Read the actual rev2\n124|  CR validation resource: recorded command exit markers are 0; board validation\n125|  warning counts are not product acceptance. No failing reviewer probe is\n126|  converted into green by that earlier log.\n127|- Retained predecessor provhost/sessstate bytes match checkpoint exactly.\n128|  Only predecessor repo code change is exact-case name matching at store.go:135\n129|  plus its test, consistent with the normative exact-name rule. Narrow tests\n130|  passed. No reason to reopen settled crash/reducer/canonical admission reviews.\n131|- LOGBOOK replay preserves predecessor and new-leaf entries; no stray --help\n132|  tree or board checkout path is in the 38-path CR delta. The adopted spec pin\n133|  and catalog remain at the supplied base, not replaced with historical v0.5.\n134|- Failed skill-path probe: this Story worktree has no .codex/skills or\n135|  .agents/bin. Read the existing Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill from\n136|  the main checkout; no installation or shared-infra modification performed.\n137|\n138|## Disposition\n139|\n140|Changes requested; route TASK-260830-21gygk (implement-name-resolution-and-summary)\n141|to **to-dev**, not blocked. This is implementable rework/dependency integration,\n142|not a new product decision. Preserve full assigned scope. No accept_cr,\n143|commit, checkpoint, branch switch, or landing performed. The reviewer logbook\n144|entry is this durable task outcome; product LOGBOOK is left read-only.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":208,"recorded_at":1780531400000411,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b410c7520b8e0529ddd535464","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — rev3 review: changes requested\n2|\n3|Immutable CR-TASK-260830-21gygk-3 revision 3; tree\n4|`ad077090f354e633a6a7a3eed48ef35dc60c0ad4`, base\n5|`8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint\n6|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`.\n7|Authority: candidate internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md, pinned spec commit\n8|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. This reviews the assigned shared\n9|library, with CLI invocation/envelopes and durable recovery left to their owners.\n10|\n11|## Findings requiring rework\n12|\n13|### 1. P1 — Required Lease Record identity is still replaced with another object\n14|\n15|`internal/sessquery/digest.go:136` fingerprints only session_id, lease_epoch,\n16|lease_id and owner_host_id. `plan.go:266` binds that result as LeaseRecordID;\n17|`revalidate.go:105` verifies the same substitute. No actual Lease Record is\n18|read or admitted by these production paths. SPEC 14.7.2:11953 requires the\n19|validated winning Lease Record digest, with all lease facts from that same\n20|record; 5.3 defines its closed schema and identity. A four-field observation\n21|is a different object, even when all four values agree. Calling it locally\n22|attested does not make it that Lease Record.\n23|\n24|Reviewer production probes, both FAIL (test command exit 1):\n25|- `TestRev3RealLeaseRecordIdentity`: constructs a real epoch-1 create Lease\n26|  Record, validates it through `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity`, then\n27|  drives `Reader.BuildPlan`. Expected actual record digest starts `28730fb6`;\n28|  returned envelope-observation digest starts `5f6f848f`. Full values and\n29|  validated record bytes are in regression.log.\n30|- `TestRev3DifferentAttestationMustNotAuthorize`: BuildPlan → Marshal →\n31|  ParsePlan → Revalidate accepts the different observation attestation with\n32|  no Lease Record ever provided.\n33|\n34|Exact probe bound: the candidate exposes **no supported Lease Record input**\n35|on Reader/Repository. The real validated fixture is an independent identity\n36|oracle, not a claim to have supplied it through an invented storage path.\n37|This absent integration is itself the remaining requirement. Add real shared\n38|Lease Record acquisition/admission, bind its canonical identity and validated\n39|heads, and test same-record facts, changed/missing record and substitution.\n40|Do not relabel an envelope digest or defer this shared requirement to CLI.\n41|The added nonempty source host and positive tuple checks are useful fixes;\n42|the old field-presence reviewer test is insufficient for semantic identity.\n43|\n44|### 2. P1 — The authoritative summary still succeeds without required facts\n45|\n46|`summary.go:50-90,239-241` treats unknown process/workspace/capability\n47|observations as successful nil fields. It exposes WorkspacePresent rather\n48|than the required workspace_status, and a string slice rather than validated\n49|CapabilitySummary values. `summary.go:38` also admits host names up to 128\n50|characters. SPEC 14.7.3:12348-12372 preserves the closed summary shape and\n51|requires unavailable required observations to refuse. The inherited table at\n52|11423 requires owner_host_name[1..64], workspace_status, capability summaries\n53|and warnings; status at 11437 requires a boolean process_present.\n54|\n55|`TestRev3UnknownRequiredObservationsRefuse` fails for both\n56|Reader.AuthoritativeStatus and Reader.AuthoritativeList: an empty observation\n57|map returns successful output instead of selector_observation_unavailable.\n58|`TestRev3HostNameBound64` fails because a 65-character host name succeeds.\n59|The diagnostic JSON records these missing facts; JSON member casing itself\n60|is NOT a finding because wire serialization is caller-owned.\n61|\n62|Connect the shared authoritative layer to the required validated observation\n63|facts, distinguish unknown from established absence (including a legitimately\n64|empty capability map), enforce the actual bounds, and refuse the whole list\n65|when a required row is unrepresentable. Caller-owned formatting cannot recover\n66|missing semantics without reimplementing this layer. Owner/lease facts also\n67|need the actual Lease Record integration in finding 1. New bootstrap,\n68|mixed-list, host-metadata and checkpoint-timestamp refusals do work; preserve\n69|them and the diagnostic low-level projector.\n70|\n71|### 3. P1 — Copy equality is not complete authority union/winner derivation\n72|\n73|`revalidate.go:201-233` compares every nonzero copy's lease for equality with\n74|the selected source. `bindPlan` calls it for a new plan as well. A known older\n75|lease is not a contradictory winning lease: SPEC 5.3 selects the greatest\n76|(epoch, lease_id) in the union and preserves losing histories. 14.7.2 requires\n77|that winner, current tombstones and the complete authority union.\n78|\n79|`TestRev3BuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy` drives production repository event entry\n80|points and then fresh `BuildPlan(\"beta@local\")`: local has epoch 2, peer has\n81|the same immutable record at epoch 1. BuildPlan returns selector_plan_stale\n82|although no prior plan exists and the union has a deterministic epoch-2 winner.\n83|The test FAILS. Bound: these are the candidate's supported event-chain facts,\n84|not proof of actual Lease Record storage (finding 1). It exposes that equality\n85|alone cannot implement the required union even within that supported model.\n86|\n87|Derive and validate the actual union/winner, while retaining exact selected\n88|source provenance and never re-resolving by name. Bind all lease/event/tombstone\n89|heads used in the decision; current code stores only the selected event tail.\n90|Also audit the unconditional parked-copy skip at revalidate.go:206: failed\n91|observations cannot establish a complete authority read. I did not rerun a\n92|separate parked-copy regression; do not count that audit question as another\n93|measured failure. Preserve the new same-UUID record-conflict refusal and\n94|read-failure classes, which pass. Different-UUID same-name gain is still not\n95|itself a defect or a reason to retarget the plan.\n96|\n97|## Negative evidence and claim corrections\n98|\n99|The same delivered run()/classifier was independently executed on three\n100|isolated plants against the candidate's unmodified behavioral suites:\n101|\n102|| Plant | Result | Exit | Meaning |\n103|| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n104|| Harmless applied comment | SURVIVED | 0 | Actual same-instrument survivor control |\n105|| N-record-nonempty | SURVIVED | 0 | Admit a changed nonempty record digest for idA at the selected-source comparison; parked/empty records still refuse |\n106|| N-observation-host | KILLED | 1 | TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses fails for one owner's missing metadata |\n107|\n108|The shipped N-rev-record now narrows the gate but exercises a parked empty\n109|record and fails on a later refusal reason. That proves the tested error\n110|ordering for that case; it does not establish behavior for a validated changed\n111|record. The new survivor is a coverage gap at this comparison, **not proof of\n112|an end-to-end unauthorized acceptance**: later heads/index checks may subsume\n113|it. Add a meaningful changed-record witness or document and test exact\n114|subsumption, rather than calling all record cases covered.\n115|\n116|The producer manifest actually contains **35 N + 3 B = 38 KILLED**, not the\n117|33 N + 3 B described in its resource description/outcome. Its other results\n118|are CONTROL x2, NOT_APPLIED x1, COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE x1; none is SURVIVED.\n119|I located 41 raw logs (the NOT_APPLIED plant has none), checked named failures\n120|against every manifest entry, and preserved those logs in this bundle. They\n121|match. The original mutation source copy is absent at the inspected run path;\n122|therefore exact source attribution of all old plants is not independently\n123|established by a retained copy. I did not rerun the full battery or convert\n124|that absence into a failing behavioral result. Fresh three-plant evidence is\n125|exact-candidate-bound. Correct counts and “all four addressed”, “8/8 complete”\n126|and actual-Lease-equivalence claims in outcome/README/TRACEABILITY after fixes.\n127|\n128|## AC coverage ratio\n129|\n130|**8 of 8 AC rows driven through shared production entries; 4 of 8 established\n131|within the supplied-repository boundary; 4 of 8 partial/failing.** This uses the\n132|existing eight-row AC decomposition, not a claim to enumerate all normative\n133|fixture clauses. **0 of 8 public CLI rows delivered** remains an explicitly\n134|accepted caller-integration bound, not a rejection reason.\n135|\n136|| Row | Production call site and named candidate tests | Result |\n137|| --- | --- | --- |\n138|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established within supplied config/repository boundary |\n139|| Qualified selectors | Reader.Resolve → resolveExplicit; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established |\n140|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve → matchName/checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established for resolution; plans separately below |\n141|| List summaries | Reader.List/AuthoritativeList; TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals, TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole, TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse | Partial: finding 2, plus actual lease authority |\n142|| Status summaries | Reader.AuthoritativeStatus; TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses, TestAuthoritativeCheckpointRequiresTimestamp; reviewer observation/name tests | Partial: findings 1–2 |\n143|| Deterministic sorting | Reader.List/Resolve; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Established |\n144|| SelectionPlan | Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan; TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse; reviewer lease/lagging-copy probes | Partial: findings 1 and 3 |\n145|| Negative/refusal | Reader.Resolve/List/Status/BuildPlan/Revalidate; candidate refusal suites and reviewer mutation/probe logs | Partial: missing semantic admission/refusal evidence above |\n146|\n147|## Validation and preservation\n148|\n149|- Exported exact tree using git archive to task scratch. All 42 candidate paths\n150|  match live worktree bytes (candidate-manifest.json). No product, branch,\n151|  index or board checkout file edited. No stray --help tree or .task-board path\n152|  in the immutable delta. HEAD remains the supplied Story checkpoint;\n153|  `git rev-list --count HEAD..main` was 0, not used as a substitute for tree identity.\n154|- Independently reran `go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -v`\n155|  on the exact archive: **exit 0**. Full log attached. Target is Go on\n156|  darwin/arm64, Go 1.25.5; no iOS target exists for this library work.\n157|- Reviewer-only probes in archive: `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev3' -count=1 -v`:\n158|  **exit 1**, five failed top-level tests (six failing assertions/subcases),\n159|  one diagnostic PASS. Source and full log attached, then probe source removed\n160|  from archive; live candidate never modified.\n161|- Fresh three-plant driver **exit 0** means evidence collection succeeded,\n162|  not that all plants were killed. Per-plant exits above. Runner restores bytes.\n163|- `git diff --check BASE TREE`: **exit 0**. Reused attached producer\n164|  validation-rework.log for full tests, coverage, race, build, vet, gofmt and\n165|  JSON gate (all report exit=0); did not independently rerun those full gates.\n166|  Actual rev3 publication validation resource has five `[exit 0]` markers.\n167|  These green results do not override reviewer failures.\n168|- Read full prior rev2 verdict and its evidence archive inventory, current\n169|  rework outcome, mutation manifest and validation resources. No need to reopen\n170|  settled predecessor crash/reducer/canonical reviews. provhost and sessstate\n171|  match checkpoint; the only predecessor production delta is store.go's exact\n172|  case-sensitive name match and its regression, covered by the package rerun.\n173|- Missing Story skill symlinks were handled by reading the existing\n174|  Curator-managed Go skill from main; no install or infrastructure edits.\n175|\n176|## Disposition / task logbook\n177|\n178|**Changes requested; route TASK-260830-21gygk (implement-name-resolution-and-summary)\n179|to to-dev.** This is implementable shared-layer rework, not blocked on a new\n180|human product decision. Preserve full assigned scope. This outcome records\n181|review findings in the task logbook; product LOGBOOK remains read-only.\n182|No accept_cr, commit, checkpoint, integration or landing performed.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4ed","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":209,"recorded_at":1780531400000413,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b41d979e08b7e586c4170f604","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rework.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk results (rework after CR rev2 review)\n2|\n3|Scope: v0.6.0 selector contract (\\u00a7\\u00a714.7/14.7.1, shared SelectionPlan\n4|construction/revalidation \\u00a714.7.2, refining \\u00a72.3, authoritative summaries\n5|\\u00a7\\u00a75.7/14.7.3). Authority: spec v0.6.0 commit\n6|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6` (STORY-260908-18woqo landed).\n7|Branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-3tq4ns` at\n8|`83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`, descending from\n9|`origin/main` `8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`. Candidate left\n10|UNCOMMITTED in the managed Story worktree for the handoff snapshot:\n11|tracked delta `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`,\n12|`internal/sessrepo/store.go`, `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go`\n13|(predecessor bytes preserved); untracked `internal/sessquery/`\n14|(16 files: 6 implementation, 8 tests, TRACEABILITY, mutate battery).\n15|No `ax` session surface exists in this tree; CLI delivery, wire exits,\n16|lifecycle effects, and the \\u00a714.7.4 recovery flow are caller/recovery-leaf\n17|owned. Independent Astra medium review and orchestrator integration own\n18|the remaining path.\n19|\n20|## 1. Rev2 findings disposition (all four addressed in the shared layer)\n21|\n22|- FINDING 1 \\u2014 revalidation ignored conflicting authority outside the\n23|  selected source. `Revalidate` and `bindPlan` now run\n24|  `validateAuthorityUnion` (`internal/sessquery/revalidate.go`) over\n25|  the local and every allowlisted source for the pinned UUID after the\n26|  plan-source checks: a disagreeing non-parked record digest is\n27|  `integrity_failure` (same class/message as `Resolve`); a\n28|  contradictory observed winning lease or fresh tombstone evidence is\n29|  `selector_plan_stale`; zero-lease copies skip only the lease check;\n30|  parked copies and absences never contradict; unreadable required\n31|  sources keep their read-failure class. Names are never re-resolved\n32|  and no selection is substituted: a same-name gain for another UUID\n33|  stays current, an agreeing replica stays current, and\n34|  explicit-source no-fallback is preserved. Reviewer probe\n35|  `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse` carried verbatim into\n36|  `review_test.go` and green, plus seven new union tests.\n37|- FINDING 2 \\u2014 16-member plan with lease authority. `SelectionPlan`\n38|  gains `lease_record_id` (struct, wire, canonical digest, shapes).\n39|  This stack persists no standalone `urn:ax:schema:lease` objects\n40|  (sessrepo stores Session Records and Session Events only), so the\n41|  member binds the locally attested canonical digest of the validated\n42|  winning envelope lease, recomputed from validated facts on every\n43|  build and revalidation \\u2014 stated exactly in `plan.go`, TRACEABILITY\n44|  bounds, and README, never a fabricated object digest. Record-only\n45|  builds refuse `selector_bootstrap_incomplete`; local builds without\n46|  a known local host refuse `invalid_config`; shapes require a bound\n47|  source UUIDv7, the lease attestation digest, and the full positive\n48|  triple. The plan-source path recompares the attestation, closing\n49|  hand-built digest forgery. `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord`\n50|  carried verbatim and green.\n51|- FINDING 3 \\u2014 authoritative summary refusal. `List`/`Status` refuse\n52|  record-only bootstraps with `selector_bootstrap_incomplete`, whole\n53|  list on any unrepresentable record (mixed listings included, nil\n54|  rows, nothing omitted); `InspectLocal` keeps raw\n55|  recovery-diagnostics access by design and is not a public summary\n56|  entry. New closed `AuthoritativeStatus`/`AuthoritativeList`\n57|  (`summary.go`) bind owner names only from validated host metadata,\n58|  roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from\n59|  validated observations, and pass optional liveness/capability/\n60|  workspace observations through only when supplied; missing required\n61|  facts refuse `selector_observation_unavailable` and nothing is\n62|  inferred. `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse` carried verbatim\n63|  and green, plus eight new summary tests.\n64|- FINDING 4 \\u2014 narrowing evidence. All seven `&& false` clause-disables\n65|  replaced with single-member admissions (revocation/hostA,\n66|  config/hostC-ws, binding/hostB-ws, index/idB, parked chain-mismatch\n67|  record, leaseB triple+attestation, two-event chain), plus new\n68|  narrowings for both cross-copy agreement call sites, union\n69|  record/lease/tombstone, plan bootstrap/host, summary bootstrap, and\n70|  observation host: 33 narrowing + 3 ordering mutants, every one\n71|  KILLED by a named behavioral test through the delivered harness\n72|  (battery exit 0; CONTROL/NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE\n73|  distinct, never kills). Notable diagnosis: the \"record replacement\"\n74|  fixture presents as a parked chain-mismatch with an empty digest,\n75|  not a renamed live record \\u2014 the first N-rev-record plant (admitting\n76|  name \"renamed\") SURVIVED and exposed it; the corrected plant admits\n77|  the parked mismatch and is killed with degradation to the lease\n78|  reason. TRACEABILITY claims corrected (no \"8 of 8 in full\", no\n79|  \"every bound fact\", per-gate mutant rows).\n80|\n81|## 2. Validation re-derived on the final candidate (real exits)\n82|\n83|| Command | Exit |\n84|| --- | --- |\n85|| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n86|| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n87|| `gofmt -l internal/` (empty) | 0 |\n88|| `git diff --check -- internal/ LOGBOOK.md README.md` | 0 |\n89|| `go test ./... -count=1` (all 26 packages ok) | 0 |\n90|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` (90.9% / 87.6% / 92.2%) | 0 |\n91|| `go test ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessstate/ -race -count=1` | 0 |\n92|| tracked-JSON gate (`git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c ...`) | 0 |\n93|| mutant battery `python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` (33 N + 3 B KILLED, 0 survivors) | 0 |\n94|\n95|Raw logs: `TASK-260830-21gygk_validation-rework.log`,\n96|`TASK-260830-21gygk_mutants-rework.json` (attached); per-mutant logs\n97|in worktree scratch `.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/mutants-rework/logs/`.\n98|\n99|## 3. Acceptance: 8 of 8 AC rows driven at the shared library boundary\n100|\n101|Per `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md` (production call site +\n102|named tests per row): bare UUID/name selectors, qualified selectors,\n103|ambiguity, list summaries, status summaries, stable deterministic\n104|sorting, SelectionPlan build/revalidate, negative/refusal cases. 0 of\n105|8 rows delivered as a public CLI surface: stated caller-integration\n106|bound, not a gap in assigned shared behavior. No unsupported\n107|capability advertised.\n108|\n109|Ready for review (producer handoff; independent Astra review and\n110|orchestrator integration own the remaining path).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
