{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c609","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":351,"recorded_at":1780531400000697,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0886b-8182-7cf2-b757-faee5e02bb72"},"task_id":"01a0886b-8182-7cf2-b757-faee5e02bb72","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0886b-8182-7cf2-b757-faee5e02bb72","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/plan.go`.\n1|// Immutable SelectionPlan construction and current-fact revalidation\n2|// for the v0.6.0 selector contract (SPEC Section 14.7.2).\n3|//\n4|// Resolve the key to a session UUID once per invocation or confirmed\n5|// plan, then bind the selection facts into a machine-local immutable\n6|// plan: the literal selector, the selected session and its validated\n7|// immutable record digest, the selected source (host and exact alias),\n8|// the digests of the complete validated index read and the effective\n9|// validated configuration, the validated winning lease facts, the\n10|// validated authority heads, and the caller-declared action,\n11|// destination, and expectations. No plan hash, name, source, or display\n12|// field is a capability. All sixteen contract members bind; a future\n13|// member without a bound row fails its publication gate closed instead\n14|// of falling into a default.\n15|//\n16|// This stack persists no standalone urn:ax:schema:lease objects:\n17|// sessrepo stores Session Records and Session Events only, and the\n18|// validated winning lease is the envelope triple observed on the\n19|// authoritative event chain through the accepted projector. The plan\n20|// therefore binds lease_record_id as the locally attested canonical\n21|// digest of that validated winning-lease observation (session, epoch,\n22|// lease ID, owner), and the lease triple binds from the same\n23|// observation. The digest is recomputed from validated facts on every\n24|// build and revalidation; no digest is fabricated and no placeholder\n25|// stands in for a missing lease. A complete read proving a record\n26|// without any valid lease refuses selector_bootstrap_incomplete\n27|// instead of binding an empty triple, and a local selection without a\n28|// known local host refuses invalid_config instead of binding an empty\n29|// source host.\n30|//\n31|// Revalidation rereads the current configuration and the plan's source,\n32|// validates the same immutable record, the current winning lease, and\n33|// the action prerequisites this leaf can check, compares every bound\n34|// plan fact in a fixed order, and then validates the complete\n35|// authority union for the pinned session UUID across the local and\n36|// every allowlisted source: a contradictory immutable record is\n37|// integrity failure, a contradictory winning lease or fresh tombstone\n38|// evidence is stale. A changed mapping, alias, allowlist, transport,\n39|// source index, record, authority head, lease, action, destination, or\n40|// expectation invalidates the plan with selector_plan_stale naming the\n41|// first diverged member; explicit authorization revocation returns\n42|// peer_not_allowlisted; failed reads retain their read-failure\n43|// classification. Revalidation never re-resolves by name, substitutes\n44|// a same-named session, silently replans, transfers a lease, or reuses\n45|// confirmation for new facts.\n46|//\n47|// Effect authorization beyond read projection — fencing, commit,\n48|// retry, recovery, remote dispatch/admission, and transport-resume\n49|// prerequisites, and the composed per-endpoint invocation bindings —\n50|// belongs to the CLI and lifecycle owners, which invoke Revalidate at\n51|// every boundary in BoundariesFor for their action. A plan built here\n52|// authorizes read projection only.\n53|package sessquery\n54|\n55|import (\n56|\t\"fmt\"\n57|\n58|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n59|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n60|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n61|)\n62|\n63|// SelectorVersion is the exact selector contract version every plan binds.\n64|const SelectorVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n65|\n66|// Plan actions admitted by the Section 14.7.2 boundary matrix. Each is\n67|// an existing command/action tag; binding one selects it, never an\n68|// umbrella bypass.\n69|const (\n70|\tActionStatus      = \"status\"\n71|\tActionAttach      = \"attach\"\n72|\tActionTakeover    = \"takeover\"\n73|\tActionFork        = \"fork\"\n74|\tActionStop        = \"stop\"\n75|\tActionResume      = \"resume\"\n76|\tActionSync        = \"sync\"\n77|\tActionDiff        = \"diff\"\n78|\tActionMaterialize = \"materialize\"\n79|\tActionSetProfile  = \"session.set-profile\"\n80|\tActionLogs        = \"logs\"\n81|\tActionCancel      = \"cancel\"\n82|)\n83|\n84|// Plan boundaries from the normative action/boundary matrix. A boundary\n85|// is reached only when the existing operation reaches that phase; these\n86|// rows introduce no new effects.\n87|const (\n88|\tBoundaryProjection      = \"projection\"\n89|\tBoundaryPreEffect       = \"pre-effect\"\n90|\tBoundaryFencing         = \"fencing\"\n91|\tBoundaryCommit          = \"commit\"\n92|\tBoundaryRetry           = \"retry\"\n93|\tBoundaryRecovery        = \"recovery\"\n94|\tBoundaryRemoteDispatch  = \"remote-dispatch\"\n95|\tBoundaryRemoteAdmission = \"remote-admission\"\n96|\tBoundaryTransportResume = \"transport-resume\"\n97|)\n98|\n99|// planBoundaries is the closed action/boundary matrix: every action has\n100|// exactly its normative row, and an unknown action has none.\n101|var planBoundaries = map[string][]string{\n102|\tActionStatus:      {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n103|\tActionAttach:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n104|\tActionTakeover:    {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n105|\tActionFork:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n106|\tActionStop:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n107|\tActionResume:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n108|\tActionSync:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n109|\tActionDiff:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n110|\tActionMaterialize: {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n111|\tActionSetProfile:  {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n112|\tActionLogs:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n113|\tActionCancel:      {BoundaryProjection},\n114|}\n115|\n116|// BoundariesFor returns the required boundary classes for a plan\n117|// action. The boolean reports whether the action is a known tag; an\n118|// unknown action binds no boundary and builds no plan.\n119|func BoundariesFor(action string) ([]string, bool) {\n120|\tboundaries, ok := planBoundaries[action]\n121|\tif !ok {\n122|\t\treturn nil, false\n123|\t}\n124|\treturn append([]string(nil), boundaries...), true\n125|}\n126|\n127|// SelectionPlan is the machine-local immutable binding of one selector\n128|// resolution. All members are values, never references: there is no\n129|// mutator, and Marshal carries the locally verified canonical digest\n130|// so a persisted plan is tamper-evident. Caller-supplied digest\n131|// equality alone is never evidence of authority; only Revalidate\n132|// against current facts decides currency.\n133|type SelectionPlan struct {\n134|\t// SelectorVersion is exactly SelectorVersion.\n135|\tSelectorVersion string\n136|\t// Selector is the original single argument, at most\n137|\t// MaxSelectorRunes characters.\n138|\tSelector string\n139|\t// SessionID is the selected UUIDv7, never resolved again by name.\n140|\tSessionID string\n141|\t// SessionRecordID is the validated immutable Session Record digest.\n142|\tSessionRecordID string\n143|\t// SourceHostID is the UUIDv7 of the selected source, always bound:\n144|\t// a local selection without a known local host refuses\n145|\t// invalid_config at build time instead of binding empty.\n146|\tSourceHostID string\n147|\t// SourceAlias is the exact configured alias, or nil for local. It\n148|\t// is a diagnostic label, never identity.\n149|\tSourceAlias *string\n150|\t// SourceIndexDigest is the digest of the complete validated index\n151|\t// read used for selection.\n152|\tSourceIndexDigest string\n153|\t// ConfigurationDigest is the digest of the effective validated\n154|\t// configuration, including peer mapping, allowlist, and transport.\n155|\tConfigurationDigest string\n156|\t// LeaseRecordID is the locally attested canonical digest of the\n157|\t// validated winning-lease observation (session, epoch, lease ID,\n158|\t// owner). This stack persists no standalone Lease Record objects;\n159|\t// the observation is the envelope triple on the authoritative\n160|\t// event chain, and the digest is recomputed from validated facts,\n161|\t// never fabricated and never a placeholder.\n162|\tLeaseRecordID string\n163|\t// LeaseEpoch, LeaseID, and OwnerHostID come from the same validated\n164|\t// winning-lease observation as LeaseRecordID: positive uint53,\n165|\t// UUIDv4, and UUIDv7. A plan with no observed winning lease is\n166|\t// never built; the builder refuses selector_bootstrap_incomplete.\n167|\tLeaseEpoch  uint64\n168|\tLeaseID     string\n169|\tOwnerHostID string\n170|\t// AuthorityHeads is the sorted unique digest array of the\n171|\t// validated event heads used for the decision: the tail event\n172|\t// digest of the selected validated chain.\n173|\tAuthorityHeads []string\n174|\t// Action is the explicit command/action tag bound at build time.\n175|\tAction string\n176|\t// DestinationHostID is the explicit destination UUIDv7, or nil\n177|\t// when the action takes no destination.\n178|\tDestinationHostID *string\n179|\t// ExpectationDigest binds the caller-declared action expectations\n180|\t// (canonically encoded JSON) for change detection. It does not\n181|\t// replace the checkpoint, workspace, cohort, provider, terminal,\n182|\t// or confirmation contracts, which have no owners in this leaf.\n183|\tExpectationDigest string\n184|}\n185|\n186|// PlanArgs declares the invocation facts BuildPlan binds: the literal\n187|// selector, the explicit action tag, the explicit destination (empty\n188|// for none), and the opaque caller expectations (nil for none).\n189|type PlanArgs struct {\n190|\tSelector     string\n191|\tAction       string\n192|\tDestination  string\n193|\tExpectations []byte\n194|}\n195|\n196|// BuildPlan resolves the selector once through the shared path and\n197|// binds the current facts into an immutable plan. The destination is\n198|// independently validated as a UUIDv7; expectations must be canonically\n199|// encodable JSON and bind by digest for change detection only.\n200|func (reader *Reader) BuildPlan(args PlanArgs) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n201|\tparsed, err := ParseSelector(args.Selector)\n202|\tif err != nil {\n203|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n204|\t}\n205|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n206|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n207|\t}\n208|\tconfig, err := reader.validatedConfiguration()\n209|\tif err != nil {\n210|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n211|\t}\n212|\tif _, ok := BoundariesFor(args.Action); !ok {\n213|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unknown plan action %q\", ErrInvalidArgument, args.Action)\n214|\t}\n215|\tvar destination *string\n216|\tif args.Destination != \"\" {\n217|\t\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(args.Destination)\n218|\t\tif err != nil {\n219|\t\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed destination host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n220|\t\t}\n221|\t\tvalue := id.String()\n222|\t\tdestination = &value\n223|\t}\n224|\texpectations, err := fingerprintExpectations(args.Expectations)\n225|\tif err != nil {\n226|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n227|\t}\n228|\tvar selected Selection\n229|\tif parsed.Source != SourceBare {\n230|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveExplicit(parsed, config)\n231|\t} else {\n232|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveBare(parsed, config)\n233|\t}\n234|\tif err != nil {\n235|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n236|\t}\n237|\treturn reader.bindPlan(parsed, config, selected, args.Action, destination, expectations)\n238|}\n239|\n240|// bindPlan reads the winning source completely and binds every plan\n241|// member from validated current facts. The session is located by its\n242|// UUID in the winning source only, never re-resolved by name.\n243|func (reader *Reader) bindPlan(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig, selected Selection, action string, destination *string, expectations string) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n244|\trows, err := reader.readSource(selected.repo, selected.PeerHostID)\n245|\tif err != nil {\n246|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n247|\t}\n248|\tindex, err := fingerprintIndex(reader, selected.repo, rows, selected.PeerHostID)\n249|\tif err != nil {\n250|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n251|\t}\n252|\tconfiguration, err := fingerprintConfiguration(reader, config)\n253|\tif err != nil {\n254|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n255|\t}\n256|\tvar recordID string\n257|\tfound := false\n258|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n259|\t\tif row.Projection.SessionID == selected.SessionID {\n260|\t\t\trecordID, found = row.Projection.RecordID, true\n261|\t\t\tbreak\n262|\t\t}\n263|\t}\n264|\tif !found {\n265|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: selection absent from source index\", ErrPlanStale)\n266|\t}\n267|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n268|\tif err != nil {\n269|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n270|\t}\n271|\tif projection.Winner.IsZero() {\n272|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: complete authority read proves record %s without any valid lease\", ErrBootstrapIncomplete, selected.SessionID)\n273|\t}\n274|\tleaseRecordID, err := fingerprintWinningLease(selected.SessionID, projection.Winner.Epoch, projection.Winner.LeaseID, projection.OwnerHostID)\n275|\tif err != nil {\n276|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n277|\t}\n278|\ttail, err := chainTail(selected.repo, selected.SessionID)\n279|\tif err != nil {\n280|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n281|\t}\n282|\tplan := SelectionPlan{\n283|\t\tSelectorVersion:     SelectorVersion,\n284|\t\tSelector:            parsed.Raw,\n285|\t\tSessionID:           selected.SessionID,\n286|\t\tSessionRecordID:     recordID,\n287|\t\tSourceIndexDigest:   index,\n288|\t\tConfigurationDigest: configuration,\n289|\t\tLeaseRecordID:       leaseRecordID,\n290|\t\tLeaseEpoch:          projection.Winner.Epoch,\n291|\t\tLeaseID:             projection.Winner.LeaseID,\n292|\t\tOwnerHostID:         projection.OwnerHostID,\n293|\t\tAction:              action,\n294|\t\tDestinationHostID:   destination,\n295|\t\tExpectationDigest:   expectations,\n296|\t}\n297|\tif selected.PeerHostID == \"\" {\n298|\t\tif config.localHost == \"\" {\n299|\t\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local host identity is required to bind a local plan source\", ErrInvalidConfig)\n300|\t\t}\n301|\t\tplan.SourceHostID = config.localHost\n302|\t} else {\n303|\t\tplan.SourceHostID = selected.PeerHostID\n304|\t\t// Null marks the local source only. An alias-less peer binds\n305|\t\t// empty: the host still distinguishes it from local.\n306|\t\talias := config.aliasFor(selected.PeerHostID)\n307|\t\taliasCopy := alias\n308|\t\tplan.SourceAlias = &aliasCopy\n309|\t}\n310|\tif tail != \"\" {\n311|\t\tplan.AuthorityHeads = []string{tail}\n312|\t} else {\n313|\t\tplan.AuthorityHeads = []string{}\n314|\t}\n315|\tif err := checkPlanShapes(plan); err != nil {\n316|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n317|\t}\n318|\tif err := reader.validateAuthorityUnion(plan, config, selected.PeerHostID); err != nil {\n319|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n320|\t}\n321|\treturn plan, nil\n322|}\n323|\n324|// chainTail returns the tail event digest of a validated session chain,\n325|// or empty when the chain carries no events yet.\n326|func chainTail(repo *sessrepo.Repository, sessionID string) (string, error) {\n327|\tevents, err := repo.ListEvents(sessionID)\n328|\tif err != nil {\n329|\t\treturn \"\", err\n330|\t}\n331|\tif len(events) == 0 {\n332|\t\treturn \"\", nil\n333|\t}\n334|\treturn events[len(events)-1].EventID, nil\n335|}","final_result":true}}}
