{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c693","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":420,"recorded_at":1780531400000835,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b93b87630bbd1f08d98d333ea","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/query.go`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|\t\t}\n501|\t\tif !seen {\n502|\t\t\tdigest, seen = item.summary.Projection.RecordID, true\n503|\t\t\tcontinue\n504|\t\t}\n505|\t\tif item.summary.Projection.RecordID != digest {\n506|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: session %s carries disagreeing record digests across sources\", sessstate.ErrIntegrity, won.SessionID)\n507|\t\t}\n508|\t}\n509|\treturn nil\n510|}\n511|\n512|func (reader *Reader) peerCandidates() ([]candidate, error) {\n513|\tids := append([]string(nil), reader.AllowlistedPeerIDs...)\n514|\tsort.Strings(ids)\n515|\tvar out []candidate\n516|\tfor index, id := range ids {\n517|\t\tif index > 0 && id == ids[index-1] {\n518|\t\t\tcontinue\n519|\t\t}\n520|\t\tvar repo *sessrepo.Repository\n521|\t\tfound := false\n522|\t\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n523|\t\t\tif peer.HostID != id {\n524|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n525|\t\t\t}\n526|\t\t\tif found {\n527|\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: multiple indexes for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, id)\n528|\t\t\t}\n529|\t\t\tfound = true\n530|\t\t\trepo = peer.Repo\n531|\t\t}\n532|\t\t// An allowlisted peer with no learned index contributes no learned names.\n533|\t\t// A listed index with an unavailable repository is a failed observation.\n534|\t\tif !found {\n535|\t\t\tcontinue\n536|\t\t}\n537|\t\tif repo == nil {\n538|\t\t\treturn nil, peerReadFailed(id, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unreadable index for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, id))\n539|\t\t}\n540|\t\trows, err := reader.read(repo)\n541|\t\tif err != nil {\n542|\t\t\treturn nil, peerReadFailed(id, err)\n543|\t\t}\n544|\t\tout = append(out, liveCandidates(rows, repo, id)...)\n545|\t}\n546|\treturn out, nil\n547|}\n548|\n549|func matchName(items []candidate, selector string) (Selection, bool, error) {\n550|\t// A replicated session is one identity, regardless of how many peers learned\n551|\t// it. Distinct session IDs in the folded bucket are an ambiguity.\n552|\tids := make(map[string]struct{})\n553|\tvar exact *Selection\n554|\tfor _, item := range items {\n555|\t\tif asciiFold(item.summary.Projection.Name) != asciiFold(selector) {\n556|\t\t\tcontinue\n557|\t\t}\n558|\t\tids[item.selection.SessionID] = struct{}{}\n559|\t\tif item.summary.Projection.Name == selector && exact == nil {\n560|\t\t\tselection := item.selection\n561|\t\t\texact = &selection\n562|\t\t}\n563|\t}\n564|\tif len(ids) > 1 {\n565|\t\treturn Selection{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: name %q collides across %d sessions\", ErrAmbiguous, selector, len(ids))\n566|\t}\n567|\tif exact != nil {\n568|\t\treturn *exact, true, nil\n569|\t}\n570|\treturn Selection{}, false, nil\n571|}\n572|\n573|func asciiFold(value string) string {\n574|\tfolded := []byte(value)\n575|\tfor index, character := range folded {\n576|\t\tif character >= 'A' && character <= 'Z' {\n577|\t\t\tfolded[index] += 'a' - 'A'\n578|\t\t}\n579|\t}\n580|\treturn string(folded)\n581|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c695","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":421,"recorded_at":1780531400000837,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b94da71e2ae32596dd7d18819","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/selector.go`.\n1|// Selector grammar and configured source validation for the v0.6.0\n2|// session selector contract (SPEC Section 14.7.1, refining Section 2.3).\n3|//\n4|// A selector is one CLI argument. The split is at the FIRST literal \"@\"\n5|// only: the key is a session NAME, a bare UUID, or \"id:SESSION_UUID\", and\n6|// the source is empty (bare Section 2.3 tiers), \"local\",\n7|// \"peer:ALIAS\" (the entire remaining suffix, literal), or\n8|// \"id:HOST_UUID\". The parser never joins arguments, decodes percent\n9|// escapes, normalizes Unicode, trims, or case-folds aliases: a percent\n10|// sign, surrounding spaces, or a second \"@\" inside a peer alias are\n11|// literal characters of that alias.\n12|//\n13|// Configuration (local host identity, peer alias/host mappings, peer\n14|// allowlist) arrives from the owning configuration layer together with\n15|// the learned index handles, exactly as Reader documents. The selector\n16|// validates the effective configuration it is given — including exact\n17|// alias and host-ID uniqueness — because a caller-supplied mapping is\n18|// not independently attested here. Duplicate source mappings are\n19|// invalid configuration, never first-match selection.\n20|package sessquery\n21|\n22|import (\n23|\t\"fmt\"\n24|\t\"sort\"\n25|\t\"strings\"\n26|\t\"unicode\"\n27|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n28|\n29|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n30|)\n31|\n32|// MaxSelectorRunes bounds one selector argument: 64 NAME characters plus\n33|// \"@\" plus \"peer:\" plus a 64-character alias, counted in runes so a\n34|// Unicode alias keeps its configured 64-character allowance.\n35|const MaxSelectorRunes = 134\n36|\n37|// MaxAliasRunes is the existing configured peer-name bound (1-64\n38|// printable characters) this grammar reuses without adding an alias\n39|// encoding, normalization, or registration path.\n40|const MaxAliasRunes = 64\n41|\n42|// Selector source kinds. SourceBare retains the exact Section 2.3\n43|// tiers; every other kind selects in exactly one source index with no\n44|// fallback to any other source.\n45|type SelectorSource int\n46|\n47|const (\n48|\t// SourceBare resolves local exact name, allowlisted peer exact\n49|\t// name, exact UUID, then not found.\n50|\tSourceBare SelectorSource = iota\n51|\t// SourceLocal selects only in the local derived source index.\n52|\tSourceLocal\n53|\t// SourcePeerAlias selects only in the configured peer source\n54|\t// whose entire remaining suffix is the literal alias.\n55|\tSourcePeerAlias\n56|\t// SourcePeerHost selects only in the source whose canonical host\n57|\t// UUID is given; the local UUID selects local, otherwise exactly\n58|\t// one allowlisted configured peer.\n59|\tSourcePeerHost\n60|)\n61|\n62|// Selector is one parsed selector argument: the literal raw text, the\n63|// key before the first \"@\", and the source after it.\n64|type Selector struct {\n65|\t// Raw is the original single argument, preserved verbatim for plan\n66|\t// binding: another spelling that resolves to the same session never\n67|\t// authorizes the same plan.\n68|\tRaw string\n69|\t// Key is the literal text before the first \"@\", or the whole\n70|\t// argument when it carries no \"@\".\n71|\tKey string\n72|\t// IDKey reports the \"id:\" key form, which bypasses names and never\n73|\t// denotes a provider-native ID, directory instance ID, lease ID,\n74|\t// or UUID prefix.\n75|\tIDKey bool\n76|\t// UUIDShaped reports a key that parses as a canonical UUIDv7. A\n77|\t// bare UUID-shaped key still tries exact names first (Section 2.3\n78|\t// name-first precedence); a qualified UUID-shaped NAME tries the\n79|\t// exact name in its source first, then the UUID.\n80|\tUUIDShaped bool\n81|\t// Source is the selector source kind.\n82|\tSource SelectorSource\n83|\t// SourceValue is the literal peer alias (SourcePeerAlias) or the\n84|\t// canonical host UUID (SourcePeerHost), and empty otherwise.\n85|\tSourceValue string\n86|}\n87|\n88|// ParseSelector applies the literal grammar to one selector argument.\n89|// A percent sign in an alias is literal. \"peer:\" with an empty alias,\n90|// unknown source prefixes, malformed durable IDs, an empty key, and an\n91|// overlong argument are invalid arguments, never silent names.\n92|func ParseSelector(argument string) (Selector, error) {\n93|\tif utf8.RuneCountInString(argument) > MaxSelectorRunes {\n94|\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: selector exceeds %d characters\", ErrInvalidArgument, MaxSelectorRunes)\n95|\t}\n96|\tkey, source, qualified := strings.Cut(argument, \"@\")\n97|\tif key == \"\" {\n98|\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: selector carries an empty key\", ErrInvalidArgument)\n99|\t}\n100|\tparsed := Selector{Raw: argument, Key: key}\n101|\tif id, ok := strings.CutPrefix(key, \"id:\"); ok {\n102|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(id); err != nil {\n103|\t\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed id: session UUID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n104|\t\t}\n105|\t\tparsed.IDKey = true\n106|\t\tparsed.UUIDShaped = true\n107|\t} else if _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(key); err == nil {\n108|\t\tparsed.UUIDShaped = true\n109|\t}\n110|\tif !qualified {\n111|\t\tparsed.Source = SourceBare\n112|\t\treturn parsed, nil\n113|\t}\n114|\tswitch {\n115|\tcase source == \"local\":\n116|\t\tparsed.Source = SourceLocal\n117|\tcase strings.HasPrefix(source, \"peer:\"):\n118|\t\talias := strings.TrimPrefix(source, \"peer:\")\n119|\t\tif err := checkAlias(alias); err != nil {\n120|\t\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed peer alias: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n121|\t\t}\n122|\t\tparsed.Source = SourcePeerAlias\n123|\t\tparsed.SourceValue = alias\n124|\tcase strings.HasPrefix(source, \"id:\"):\n125|\t\thost := strings.TrimPrefix(source, \"id:\")\n126|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(host); err != nil {\n127|\t\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed id: host UUID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t\tparsed.Source = SourcePeerHost\n130|\t\tparsed.SourceValue = host\n131|\tdefault:\n132|\t\treturn Selector{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unknown selector source %q\", ErrInvalidArgument, source)\n133|\t}\n134|\treturn parsed, nil\n135|}\n136|\n137|// checkAlias enforces the existing configured peer-name bound without\n138|// normalizing: valid UTF-8, 1-64 printable non-control runes, compared\n139|// exactly everywhere it is used.\n140|func checkAlias(alias string) error {\n141|\tif !utf8.ValidString(alias) {\n142|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"alias is not valid UTF-8\")\n143|\t}\n144|\tcount := utf8.RuneCountInString(alias)\n145|\tif count < 1 || count > MaxAliasRunes {\n146|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"alias carries %d characters, want 1-%d\", count, MaxAliasRunes)\n147|\t}\n148|\tfor _, character := range alias {\n149|\t\tif unicode.IsControl(character) || !unicode.IsPrint(character) {\n150|\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"alias carries a non-printable character\")\n151|\t\t}\n152|\t}\n153|\treturn nil\n154|}\n155|\n156|// validatedConfig is the effective source configuration every selector\n157|// entry validates before reading any index: the local host, the\n158|// allowlist as a set, and the alias mapping restricted to known peer\n159|// hosts. Indexes and mappings stay separate inputs; this type only\n160|// records that the mapping shapes and uniqueness hold.\n161|type validatedConfig struct {\n162|\tlocalHost string\n163|\tallowed   map[string]struct{}\n164|\taliasOf   map[string]string\n165|}\n166|\n167|// validatedConfiguration validates the effective configuration the\n168|// caller supplied: local host shape, peer host shapes and alias\n169|// shapes, exact uniqueness of host-ID and alias mappings (including\n170|// against the local host), and allowlist ID shapes. Duplicate source\n171|// mappings are invalid configuration, never first-match selection. An\n172|// allowlisted ID without a learned index stays absence in union tiers;\n173|// it is validated for shape here and resolved at read time.\n174|func (reader *Reader) validatedConfiguration() (validatedConfig, error) {\n175|\tconfig := validatedConfig{allowed: map[string]struct{}{}, aliasOf: map[string]string{}}\n176|\tif reader == nil {\n177|\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: reader carries no configuration\", ErrInvalidConfig)\n178|\t}\n179|\tif reader.LocalHostID != \"\" {\n180|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(reader.LocalHostID); err != nil {\n181|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed local host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidConfig, err)\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t\tconfig.localHost = reader.LocalHostID\n184|\t}\n185|\t// Duplicate learned-index observations for one peer host keep their\n186|\t// existing read-time duplicate-index refusal (peerCandidates owns\n187|\t// it); configuration validation polices the mapping plane only, so\n188|\t// a peer host colliding with the local host is the duplicate\n189|\t// source mapping refused here.\n190|\tseenAliases := map[string]struct{}{}\n191|\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n192|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(peer.HostID); err != nil {\n193|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed peer host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidConfig, err)\n194|\t\t}\n195|\t\tif peer.HostID == config.localHost && config.localHost != \"\" {\n196|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: duplicate source mapping for host %s\", ErrInvalidConfig, peer.HostID)\n197|\t\t}\n198|\t}\n199|\tfor host, alias := range reader.Aliases {\n200|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(host); err != nil {\n201|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed alias host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidConfig, err)\n202|\t\t}\n203|\t\tif err := checkAlias(alias); err != nil {\n204|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %v\", ErrInvalidConfig, err)\n205|\t\t}\n206|\t\tif _, duplicate := seenAliases[alias]; duplicate {\n207|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: duplicate source mapping for alias %q\", ErrInvalidConfig, alias)\n208|\t\t}\n209|\t\tseenAliases[alias] = struct{}{}\n210|\t\tconfig.aliasOf[host] = alias\n211|\t}\n212|\tfor _, id := range reader.AllowlistedPeerIDs {\n213|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(id); err != nil {\n214|\t\t\treturn config, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed allowlisted peer ID: %v\", ErrInvalidConfig, err)\n215|\t\t}\n216|\t\tconfig.allowed[id] = struct{}{}\n217|\t}\n218|\treturn config, nil\n219|}\n220|\n221|// aliasFor reports the exact configured alias for a known peer host,\n222|// or empty when the source carries no alias mapping.\n223|func (config validatedConfig) aliasFor(host string) string {\n224|\treturn config.aliasOf[host]\n225|}\n226|\n227|// hostForAlias resolves an exact literal alias to its single host. The\n228|// comparison is exact: folding, trimming, or decoding never applies.\n229|func (config validatedConfig) hostForAlias(reader *Reader, alias string) (string, bool) {\n230|\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n231|\t\tif config.aliasOf[peer.HostID] == alias && alias != \"\" {\n232|\t\t\treturn peer.HostID, true\n233|\t\t}\n234|\t}\n235|\treturn \"\", false\n236|}\n237|\n238|// sortedPeerHosts returns the known peer hosts in bytewise order so\n239|// configuration digests and tie breaks stay deterministic.\n240|func (config validatedConfig) sortedPeerHosts(reader *Reader) []string {\n241|\thosts := make([]string, 0, len(reader.Peers))\n242|\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n243|\t\thosts = append(hosts, peer.HostID)\n244|\t}\n245|\tsort.Strings(hosts)\n246|\treturn hosts\n247|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c697","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":422,"recorded_at":1780531400000839,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"call_id":"call_01a0886b95407d708445357466711bb6","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`, adopted through\n5|STORY-260908-18woqo. Primary scope is Sections 14.7 and 14.7.1 with\n6|shared SelectionPlan construction and revalidation in 14.7.2, refining\n7|Section 2.3 and the authoritative summaries in 5.7/14.7.3. Historical\n8|scope is retained without weakening: v0.5.0 (commit\n9|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`), Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2,\n10|5.7, 14.4. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n11|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n12|\n13|The v0.6.0 adoption decides the two product questions the partial leaf\n14|left open. The qualified-selector syntax, source-peer versus\n15|winning-owner target, and precedence are now normative text in 14.7.1:\n16|split at the first literal `@`, exact configured alias or host identity\n17|as the source, Section 2.3 tiers for bare input, name-first then UUID\n18|inside one qualified source, and no explicit-source fallback. The\n19|prior stop-line packet on those questions is superseded, not\n20|re-opened. The creating/record-only routing clarification is applied:\n21|creating is a Session Record AND an authoritative initial lease\n22|(5.7/13.1 step 2); a record-only chain is an interrupted persistence\n23|prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf (14.7.4), and list/status\n24|entries refuse it with selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of\n25|returning an ownerless row.\n26|\n27|## Acceptance rows\n28|\n29|8 of 8 AC rows are driven at the shared-library production entries\n30|named below; 0 of 8 are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an\n31|explicit caller-integration bound (no `ax` session command exists in\n32|this tree), not a gap in the assigned shared behavior. CLI/Result-5\n33|delivery, wire exit binding, lifecycle effects, and the 14.7.4\n34|recovery flow belong to their owning leaves, which invoke this API at\n35|every required boundary instead of resolving again.\n36|\n37|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n38|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n39|| Bare UUID/name selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveBare` | `TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | Driven: Section 2.3 tiers preserved byte for byte, local-name-before-UUID, `id:` bypasses names for the durable union identity, replicated copies deduplicate on agreeing record digests with a bytewise host tie break. The repository-layer exact-name rule underneath the local tier stays pinned by `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at the retained `Repository.Resolve` entry in `sessrepo`, not at this call site. |\n40|| Qualified selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveExplicit` → `locateSource` | `TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex`, `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack`, `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures` | Driven: first-`@` literal grammar, `local`/`peer:` entire-suffix/`id:` host forms, single-source tiers with name-first then UUID, no fallback in either direction, unknown/disallowed/refusal classes. |\n41|| Ambiguity | `matchName`; `selectIdentity`/`checkRecordAgreement` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Driven: ASCII-fold collisions refuse within the reached tier and within one qualified source; replicated identical copies stay one identity; disagreeing record digests are integrity failure, never silent first match. Cross-copy agreement carries one narrowing mutant per call site (`N-identity-diverge`, `N-agreement-name`). |\n42|| List summaries | `Reader.List` → `Repository.ListSessions` → `Projector.Project` + `checkSummaryRepresentable` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`, `TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals`, `TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole`, `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse` | Driven: real identity, provider, owner/lease/local role where known, state, newest checkpoint ID, parked reason/retry, bytewise session-ID order. A complete read proving a record without any valid lease refuses the whole list with selector_bootstrap_incomplete, including a mixed healthy/incomplete listing; no partial rows escape and none is silently omitted. |\n43|| Status summaries | `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` → `Projector.Project` + gate; `Reader.AuthoritativeStatus/List` → `authorize` | Same list tests; `TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownLocalHostRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeCheckpointRequiresTimestamp`, `TestAuthoritativeInputValidation`, `TestAuthoritativeOptionalObservations` | Driven: named/UUID/qualified/id healthy status; record-only status refuses bootstrap_incomplete. The authoritative layer additionally binds owner display names only from validated host metadata, local roles only with a known local host, and checkpoint timestamps only from validated observations; missing required facts refuse selector_observation_unavailable. Host display names, liveness, capabilities, workspace, and sync facts stay absent unless their validated owners supply them. Explicit `InspectLocal` keeps raw access to parked/tombstoned/recovery diagnostics and is not a public summary entry. |\n44|| Stable deterministic sorting | `Reader.read`; `peerCandidates`; `selectIdentity` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Driven: bytewise session-ID list order, deterministic bytewise peer-source order with duplicate-allowlist stability, bytewise holder-host tie break for identical copies. Each ordering carries a behavioral mutant (`B-peer-order`, `B-session-order`, `B-tie-break`). |\n45|| SelectionPlan build and revalidate | `Reader.BuildPlan` → `bindPlan`; `Reader.Revalidate` (+ `validateAuthorityUnion`); `ParsePlan` | `TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts`, `TestBuildPlanPeerSourceFacts`, `TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionRefusesBootstrap`, `TestBuildPlanLocalSourceRequiresKnownHost`, `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`, `TestPlanDigestAndMarshalRoundTrip`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange`, `TestRevalidateUnionLeaseDivergenceRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionTombstoneRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionAgreeingReplicaStaysCurrent`, `TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyIgnored`, `TestRevalidateUnionUnreadablePeerRefuses`, `TestRevalidateUnionNameDriftStaysCurrent`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateMalformedPlans`, `TestActionBoundaryTable`, `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse`, `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord` | Driven: all sixteen members bound once, fixed compare order with per-member stale reasons, revocation class, cross-source integrity class, read/projection failure classes, tamper-evident persistence where digest equality never substitutes for revalidation. A same-name gain for another UUID never retargets the pinned plan; an agreeing replica never invalidates it. |\n46|| Negative and refusal cases | All gates below | Every `Test*` refusal arm plus the battery | Driven: distinct classes for invalid arguments, invalid configuration, unknown source, disallowed peer, remote read failure, ambiguity, not found, integrity failure, bootstrap incompleteness, unavailable observations, and stale plans, each killed by narrowing. No unsupported capability is advertised (see bounds). |\n47|\n48|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n49|\n50|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n51|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n52|reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the delivered\n53|harness. Whole-clause disables are not accepted as narrowing. `B-`\n54|rows reverse deterministic orderings. Controls are reported\n55|separately and never counted as kills.\n56|\n57|| Gate | Real entry test | Narrowing attack (all killed) |\n58|| --- | --- | --- |\n59|| Folded-name ambiguity | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions` | N-collision-pair admits exactly two colliding identities. |\n60|| Exact-name admission | Shared tiers: `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`; retained repository entry: `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at `Repository.Resolve` in `sessrepo` | N-case-variant admits one non-exact selector at the shared tier and is killed by the sessquery collision test; N-repository-case-variant admits one non-exact query at the retained repository entry and is killed by the sessrepo test at that entry. |\n61|| First-`@` literal split | `TestParseSelectorLiteralGrammar` | N-first-at-split keeps the `@` token and splits at the last one; an alias containing `@` misroutes. |\n62|| `local` source literal | Same | N-local-prefix keeps the token and admits `local`-prefixed sources. |\n63|| `id:` key literal | Same | N-id-case keeps the token and folds the prefix; `ID:` bypasses names. |\n64|| Alias exactness | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/alias_casing_is_exact` | N-peer-alias-fold keeps the mapping and folds comparison; `WORK` selects `Work`. |\n65|| `id:` name bypass | `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource` | N-id-through-names routes one explicit `id:` key through the name tier; a UUID-shaped name shadows the identity. |\n66|| No explicit-source fallback | `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack` | N-explicit-fallback falls back to the bare union on exactly an explicit miss. |\n67|| Unknown source refusal | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals` | N-unknown-alias-local treats exactly an unknown alias as local. |\n68|| Peer allowlist | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-disallowed-admit reads exactly one disallowed peer; N-unlisted-peer reads one unlisted identity. |\n69|| Duplicate learned index | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-duplicate-peer admits duplicates for one host ID. |\n70|| Duplicate alias mapping | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/duplicate_alias_mapping` | N-dup-alias admits duplicate mappings with last-write-wins. |\n71|| Live eligibility | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions` | N-parked-id and N-tombstoned-id admit one excluded identity each. |\n72|| Cross-copy agreement, identity tier | `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` (disagreeing-copies arm) | N-identity-diverge admits exactly the idA record disagreement in `selectIdentity`; other identities still refuse. |\n73|| Cross-copy agreement, name tier | `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` (disagreeing-name-win arm) | N-agreement-name admits exactly the idA record disagreement in `checkRecordAgreement`; other identities still refuse. |\n74|| Read failure propagation | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateUnionUnreadablePeerRefuses` | N-read-failure-fallback treats repository-path failure as empty. Missing learned index, nil known index, missing root, and non-directory root are separately driven. |\n75|| Projection failure propagation | `TestListStatusCheckpointAndPropagationFailure`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange/invalid_projection_propagates` | N-projection-failure-fallback omits one identity on failed projection instead of propagating its failure. |\n76|| Plan revocation | `.../revocation_refuses_allowlist` | N-rev-revocation admits exactly the revoked hostA peer; refusal degrades to stale configuration. |\n77|| Plan configuration binding | `.../unrelated_mapping_change_changes_configuration` | N-rev-config admits exactly the ws-alias configuration for hostC; other changes still refuse. |\n78|| Plan source binding | `.../alias_remap_changes_binding` | N-rev-binding admits exactly the ws remap onto hostB; the refusal degrades to stale configuration. |\n79|| Plan index binding | `.../unrelated_session_change_changes_index` | N-rev-index admits exactly an index containing session idB; other changes still refuse. |\n80|| Plan record binding | `.../record_replacement_changes_digest` | N-rev-record admits exactly the parked chain-mismatch record the replacement fixture presents (a replaced record.json against its chain index parks the session with an empty digest); the refusal degrades to the lease reason. |\n81|| Plan lease binding | `.../successor_lease_changes_winner` | N-rev-lease admits exactly the leaseB successor, triple and attestation together; the refusal degrades to the heads reason. |\n82|| Plan heads binding | `.../same_lease_event_changes_heads` | N-rev-heads admits exactly a two-event chain; the refusal degrades to the index reason. |\n83|| Plan absence | `.../deletion_empties_selection` | N-rev-absent-substitute rebinds exactly a deleted selection to its first listed sibling. |\n84|| Union record agreement | `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse` (also `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`) | N-union-record admits exactly the idB cross-source record disagreement; other contradictions still refuse. |\n85|| Union lease agreement | `TestRevalidateUnionLeaseDivergenceRefusesStale` | N-union-lease admits exactly the leaseB cross-source successor, triple and attestation together; other contradictions still refuse. |\n86|| Union tombstone evidence | `TestRevalidateUnionTombstoneRefusesStale` | N-union-tombstone admits exactly the idB cross-source tombstone; other tombstone evidence still refuses. |\n87|| Plan bootstrap gate | `TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionRefusesBootstrap` | N-plan-bootstrap admits exactly record-only idA past the gate; the shape backstop still refuses it with invalid_arguments. |\n88|| Plan source-host gate | `TestBuildPlanLocalSourceRequiresKnownHost` | N-plan-source-host admits exactly idA past the local-host gate; the shape backstop still refuses the empty host with invalid_arguments. |\n89|| Summary bootstrap gate | `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse`, `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`, `TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals`, `TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole` | N-summary-bootstrap admits exactly record-only idA into list/status; other interrupted prefixes still refuse. |\n90|| Summary host metadata gate | `TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses` | N-observation-host admits exactly owner hostA without metadata; other missing owners still refuse. |\n91|| Deterministic order | Order tests above | B-peer-order, B-session-order reverse list orders; B-tie-break reverses the copy tie break. |\n92|\n93|The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an\n94|isolated source copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw\n95|process exits and named failed tests, then restores and verifies the\n96|copied bytes. It has before/after green controls, a not-applied\n97|control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two prove no\n98|behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are attached on\n99|the task, never hard-coded as a green claim here. No new source-text\n100|gate lacks its token-preserving mutant: the `@`, `local`, `id:`, and\n101|alias-equality tokens each carry one.\n102|\n103|The read and revalidation entries perform no durable writes. The crash\n104|test interrupts the real repository create after record installation,\n105|inspects the parked projection, retries the byte-identical create\n106|through its owner, and observes the healed read. Repeated lists and\n107|revalidations return identical values. This establishes read\n108|idempotency and composition with existing recovery, not a new crash\n109|protocol.\n110|\n111|## Stated bounds (not implementations)\n112|\n113|- `lease_record_id` binds the locally attested canonical digest of\n114|  the validated winning envelope lease (session, epoch, lease ID,\n115|  owner) as observed on the authoritative event chain through the\n116|  accepted projector. This stack persists no standalone\n117|  `urn:ax:schema:lease` objects — sessrepo stores Session Records and\n118|  Session Events only — so there is no Lease Record object digest to\n119|  read and none is fabricated. The winning triple binds from the same\n120|  observation; a complete read proving no lease refuses\n121|  selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of binding an empty triple.\n122|- `authority_heads` binds validated event-head digests only, for the\n123|  plan source alone; the complete authority union (same record,\n124|  current tombstones, winning lease across the local and every\n125|  allowlisted source) is validated at build and at every\n126|  revalidation without rebinding heads, and unrelated index changes\n127|  stay conservative stale.\n128|- `source_host_id` is always a bound UUIDv7: a local selection\n129|  without a known local host refuses invalid_config at build time.\n130|- Wire exit binding (CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0) belongs\n131|  to its owning leaf; this library keeps refusal classes distinct and\n132|  stable under their normative spellings without registering codes.\n133|- Record-only chains keep the accepted internal projection with empty\n134|  owner/lease facts inside the projector. The list/status summary\n135|  entries refuse them, while explicit local inspection retains raw\n136|  access to the recovery diagnostics. The 14.7.4 recovery flow itself\n137|  belongs to the bootstrap leaf with the accepted projector behavior\n138|  reconciled in its scoped review; this leaf invents neither a state\n139|  nor an error for it.\n140|- Effect authorization (fencing, commit, retry, recovery, remote\n141|  dispatch/admission, transport-resume) and the composed\n142|  invocation-to-plan bindings for attach and logs belong to the CLI\n143|  and lifecycle owners, which invoke `Revalidate` at every boundary in\n144|  `BoundariesFor`. Plans built here authorize read projection only.\n145|- Reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an atomic\n146|  repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer\n147|  acquisition, cross-peer lease union, and differing replicated views\n148|  are not measured. Transports, peer authentication, freshness, mesh\n149|  union, host metadata, and observation contracts remain upstream\n150|  boundaries: configuration, learned indexes, host metadata, and\n151|  observations arrive as trusted caller inputs, and the allowlist proof\n152|  covers filtering, never attestation. The repository/projector own\n153|  record/event admission and validation. No new external provider,\n154|  filesystem durability, terminal, RPC, or CLI capability is attested.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
