{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca57","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0886a-f946-7ee0-9ec1-744b6874e305"},"sequence":902,"recorded_at":1780531400001799,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5c7b7f2-5904-46fe-8e20-ce6e123abb19"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0886d-37c8-7c32-aa1a-dec4297c440f"},"task_id":"01a0886d-37c8-7c32-aa1a-dec4297c440f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0886d-37c8-7c32-aa1a-dec4297c440f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"capability-name\\\\|workspace_status\\\\|process_present\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 40; echo \\\"===\\\"; sed -n '12354,12375p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Find capability and workspace spec\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"3139:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\\n7389:| <code>session.status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,local_role:owner&#124;replica,state:SessionState,process_present:boolean,newest_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,active_operation:ActiveOperation&#124;null}</code> |\\n11423:| <code>SessionSummary</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>name:string[1..64]</code>, <code>kind:direct&#124;task_board</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>owner_host_name:string[1..64]</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>local_role:owner&#124;replica</code>, <code>state:SessionState</code>, <code>newest_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>newest_checkpoint_created_at:timestamp&#124;null</code>, <code>workspace_status:absent&#124;current&#124;staged&#124;conflict&#124;unsupported</code>, <code>capabilities:map(capability-name,CapabilitySummary)[0..7]</code>, <code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..1024]</code> |\\n11437:| <code>status</code> | <code>{session:SessionSummary,process_present:boolean,active_operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,last_successful_sync:map(UUIDv7,timestamp)[0..1024]}</code> |\\n12363:reachability, a cached row or an absent observation cannot mint process_present,\\n===\\nEvery SessionSummary owner_host_id, lease_epoch and lease_id comes from the\\nvalidated winning Lease Record, including the initial epoch-1 create lease.\\nowner_host_name comes from validated host metadata for that holder; missing host\\nmetadata is a refusal, never the source alias. local_role compares that holder\\nwith the local host UUID. Before the first checkpoint, both newest-checkpoint\\nmembers are null; creating is valid only with an authoritative initial lease\\nand the existing eligible-bootstrap facts. A Session Record alone proves\\nidentity/provenance, not creation of an owner or a creating lifecycle. Liveness\\nand capabilities require the existing observation/evidence contracts; source\\nreachability, a cached row or an absent observation cannot mint process_present,\\nreadiness, capability, or current ownership. An unknown required observation is\\nselector_observation_unavailable. Read-only inspection never creates a lease.\\n\\nA complete read proving a record without any valid lease returns\\nselector_bootstrap_incomplete; a failed read follows the local/remote read classification above,\\nand corrupt/inconsistent authority returns integrity_failure/lease_conflict as\\napplicable. List refuses the whole success document if an encountered record\\ncannot be represented truthfully; it MUST NOT silently omit that record, invent\\nsummary fields, or use partial/unreachable_peer_ids to conceal a record-only\\nbootstrap. Existing legitimate peer-partial list semantics otherwise remain.\\n\\nStructured Error 1.4.0 keeps the exact 1.3 top-level shape and all earlier\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3127,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 782,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
